r own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTIvYjE4YmQ2YjktYWE1MS00NmUzLThiZjItZDA0NGFjYzljZTk1LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201204egc400008\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 12/2: BTC, ETH, XRP, LTC, BCH, LINK, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, XLM\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,902 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 December 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin reclaimed the $19,000 level but charts suggest BTC and altcoins may consolidate for a few days before starting the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-hits-new-all-time-high-as-crypto-market-matures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit a new all-time high}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-hits-new-all-time-high-as-crypto-market-matures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-hits-new-all-time-high-as-crypto-market-matures}}}\uc2  above $19,892 on Dec. 1. This is a significant event because it proves that the rally in 2017 was ahead of fundamentals but not a bubble. Generally, when a bubble bursts, it takes several years for the price to cross the high made during the bubble.\par \par \uc2 For example, the Japanese stock market bubble {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/dec/28/how-japan-has-fared-in-30-years-since-the-stock-market-bubble-burst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came}}}\uc2  after a high was made way back in 1989, and that level has not been conquered yet. Similarly, silver\u8217\'20\'19s high close to $50 per ounce was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/hunt-brothers-trying-to-corner-silver-market-2016-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made}}}\uc2  in 1980, and the price came close to that level only in 2011. The Nasdaq {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/business-32429413"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made}}}\uc2  its high made during the dot-com bubble in 2000, and this was only crossed in 2015.\par \par \uc2 Now that it has been established that Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) was not in a bubble, the next question in the minds of traders is: How high can BTC price go?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/b5b4e625-b353-4b18-87f6-7b22fd7d46cb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Several analysts have forecast target levels according to their assumptions and calculations. However, traders should not get carried away with lofty targets because even strong uptrends witness nerve-racking corrections. Traders should aim to trade with the major trend because it generally proves to be profitable.\par \par \uc2 The increasing interest from the institutional investors suggests that the uptrend could still have some steam left. Reports suggest that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/nydig-raises-150-million-for-two-bitcoin-investment-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took only three investors to raise $150 million}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/nydig-raises-150-million-for-two-bitcoin-investment-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/nydig-raises-150-million-for-two-bitcoin-investment-funds}}}\uc2  in two separate cryptocurrency funds by the New York Digital Investment Group. While the fundamentals look strong, do the technicals also support a further rally?\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) hit a new all-time high on Dec. 1 and quickly reversed direction, which shows profit-booking at higher levels. However, the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows that the sentiment remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the bulls purchased the intraday dip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/ed9bbd52-0c35-4456-bebe-a2f9b86aa6db.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up, and the relative strength index (RSI) in the positive territory suggests that bulls have the upper hand. The buyers will now try to propel the price above the $20,000 psychological resistance.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the momentum could pick up and the BTC/USD pair may rally to $22,727 and then to $25,000.\par \par \uc2 However, if the price turns around from the $19,500\u8211\'20\'13$20,000 resistance zone, it will suggest that the bears are aggressively selling at higher levels. In such a case, the pair may consolidate for a few days before attempting to resume the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of a break in the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum will be a slide below the 20-day exponential moving average ($17,723). The advantage will shift in favor of the bears if the pair plummets below $16,191.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) broke above the $622.807 resistance and hit an intraday high of $635.456 on Dec. 1. However, the bulls could not sustain the breakout, and that could have trapped a few aggressive buyers who closed their positions in a hurry.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/52fdc9b3-a5e3-417c-bbe0-8940f956366e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 That pulled the price back below $600. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone suggest that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 However, the inside day Doji candlestick pattern today suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears. If the bulls push the price above the overhead resistance zone, the next leg of the uptrend to $800 could be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($535), a drop to $488.134 is possible.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  closed above the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.649138 on Nov. 30, but the bulls could not capitalize on this strength. This shows that the bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/f0b8cfe4-346b-4b4d-ac56-1e3fc5432d76.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The XRP/USD pair turned down sharply on Dec. 1, but the long tail on the candlestick shows buying at lower levels. When bears sell on rallies and bulls buy on dips, it is an early sign of a range formation.\par \par \uc2 The pair has formed an inside day candlestick pattern today, which suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears about the next directional move.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $0.565, a drop to the 20-day EMA ($0.50) is possible. However, if the bulls push the price above $0.68, the pair may rally to $0.780574.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the $93.9282 resistance on Dec. 1, but the positive sign is that the bulls are buying the dips below $84.3374. This suggests that the sentiment is positive.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/64a73125-ec88-42e0-8349-dfb9420d2d7e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising moving averages and the RSI above 61 suggest that the bulls are in control. If the price sustains above $84.3374, the bulls will make another attempt to clear the overhead resistance.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the next leg of the up-move to $100 may begin. Conversely, if the price turns down from the overhead resistance, a few more days of range-bound action is possible.\par \par \uc2 A break below the 20-day EMA ($76) will be the first indication that the bears are making a comeback.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not push Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) above the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $324.01 on Nov. 30 and Dec. 1. This attracted profit-booking, and the altcoin plunged to the 20-day EMA ($283).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/ddb5a246-9b60-4cd8-94ee-1b2350d48ccf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The weak rebound off the 20-day EMA suggests a lack of urgency among the bulls to buy at the current levels. If the BCH/USD pair does not pick up momentum, the possibility of a break below the $280 support increases.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 50-day simple moving average, the pair could drop to $246.85 and then to $231. This negative view will be invalidated if the pair picks up momentum and rises above $324.01. If that happens, a rally to $344.98, then to $371.70, will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink's LINK rose above the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $14.4433 on Dec. 1, but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels. This suggests that bears are selling on minor rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/cd9b11f5-25f3-43f6-b487-f9c583d8bde3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the failure of the bears to sink and sustain the price below the $13.28 support shows that lower levels are attracting buyers. The flat 20-day EMA ($13.43) and the RSI close to the midpoint suggest a few days of range-bound action.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls push the price above $14.8328, the LINK/USD pair could rise to $16.39. A breakout of this resistance could see the momentum pick up. On the contrary, if the bears sink the price below $13.28, a retest of the 50-day SMA ($12.34) is possible.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot's DOT turned down from $5.5429 on Dec. 1, which shows that the bears are aggressively defending the $5.5899 resistance. However, a minor positive is that the altcoin has bounced off the 20-day EMA ($5.04).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/dfe731f0-32ba-477c-b5aa-699fff66d973.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The gradually upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI above 57 suggest a minor advantage to the bulls. The buyers will now again try to propel the price above the $5.5899 \u8211\'20\'13$6.0857 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the next leg of the uptrend to $6.8619, then to $7.64, may begin. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA. In such a case, the DOT/USD pair could drop to the 50-day SMA ($4.56).\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The bears are defending the $0.175 level in Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The failure to rise above this resistance attracted profit-booking on Dec. 1 and pulled the price down to the 20-day EMA ($0.140).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/b979b808-0aef-490d-afad-6e33dac578ba.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are aggressively buying the dips to the 20-day EMA and are trying to keep the price above $0.155. If they manage to sustain the price above this level, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair may again reach $0.175.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from this resistance, a few days of range-bound action is possible. On the other hand, if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the correction could deepen to the 50-day SMA ($0.115).\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the $32 overhead resistance on Dec. 1 and corrected to the moving averages. This shows that the bears are defending this resistance, as they want to keep the altcoin range-bound between $25.6652 and $32.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/b77bc175-0979-427b-a157-cbf60c9f62b3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Although the bulls purchased the dip to the moving averages on Dec. 1, they have not been able to sustain the buying pressure today. This suggests hesitation to buy near the overhead resistance.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the moving averages, the BNB/USD pair could drop to $25.6652.\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI above 51 do not indicate a major advantage to either the bulls or the bears. Hence, a few days of range-bound action is possible.\par \par \uc2 XLM/USD\par \par \uc2 Failure of the bulls to push the price above the downtrend line attracted profit-booking in Stellar Lumens ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM}}}\uc2  ) on Dec. 1. However, the bears are not able to sustain the lower levels, as seen from the long tail on the candlestick.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-12/2b34d1e4-10ff-4468-b26a-bbc325b4d0db.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XLM/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XLMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The inside day candlestick pattern today suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears about the next directional move. If the bulls again fail to propel the price above the downtrend line, a deeper correction to the 20-day EMA ($.0.15) is possible.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up, and the RSI is in the positive zone. This suggests that the sentiment is positive and the bulls may buy the dips to the 20-day EMA. A strong rebound off this level could keep the XLM/USD pair range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 A break above the downtrend line will signal strength and could result in a retest of the Nov. 25 high at $0.231655.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTIvMTRhMTNkOTQtYzliYS00MWZkLThhN2UtMWU1NjlhMTdkMWNmLmpwZWc=.jpeg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201202egc2000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/30: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOT, BNB, XLM\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,664 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin broke out to secure a new 2020 high at $19,863 and altcoins look ready to follow BTC higher.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price came within striking distance of hitting a new all-time high today. This shows that institutional and retail investors continue to buy on every dip and BTC is in a strong uptrend. Hence, traders should not urgently looking to call a top.\par \par \uc2 While Bitcoin has been creating new records, gold has corrected about 15% from its all-time high. This shows that traders are dumping their positions and this led to the largest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/record-gold-outflow-isn-t-going-into-ripples-only-bitcoin-says-fund-manager"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weekly outflow}}}\uc2  in gold.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/de633043-2090-40a5-a2d2-3554d1239dbf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe that some of the money flowing out of gold could enter Bitcoin as institutional interest continues to soar. A new high could also attract momentum traders who like to piggyback on a strong trend.\par \par \uc2 Traders are now wondering if Bitcoin's momentum will pull the whole crypto sector higher or if it will continue to hog the limelight at the expense of the altcoins?\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Corrections in a strong uptrend usually last for one to three days and that is what happened with Bitcoin price. The pullback from the intraday high of $19,459.22 on Nov. 25 bottomed out at $16,191.02 on Nov. 26.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/83dfc3ec-1c2f-48b9-aac4-5540d27c92f5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A shallow correction is generally a sign of strength. It shows that existing owners of the BTC/USD pair are in no hurry to book profits while traders who want to buy are not waiting for lower levels to enter.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the relative strength index near the overbought zone suggest that bulls are in command. The momentum picked up today and the bulls pushed the price above $19,459.22.\par \par \uc2 But the bears have not yet given up. They are trying to mount a stiff resistance in the $19,500 to $20,000 zone. If the price turns down sharply from this resistance, a drop to $17,200 is possible.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the bulls can push the price above $20,000, the momentum could pick up further and a rally to $22,727 and then to $25,000 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) strong rebound off the $488.134 support shows that the bulls are buying aggressively as they expect the next leg of the uptrend to resume.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/08cf6278-f0e0-44e5-a89d-d302e56f331d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $625, the ETH/USD pair could start its journey towards the next major resistance at $800. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI near the overbought territory suggest that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price again turns down from $625, the pair may consolidate for a few days before resuming its up-move. A break below the 20-day exponential moving average ($523) will be the first sign of weakness.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The pullback in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  had been facing resistance at the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.649138 for the past two days. Today, the bulls pushed the price above the resistance but failed to sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/ad982bb8-af7d-4941-8430-0110ea4aa22b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the overbought territory suggest that bulls have the upper hand. If they can push the price above $0.649138, the XRP/USD pair could rally to $0.706942 and then to $0.780574.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price turns down from either overhead resistance and plummets below the 20-day EMA ($0.47).\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) rose above $280 on Nov. 29 and has picked up momentum today. However, the relief rally could face resistance at the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $324.01.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7f4159ed-5ff3-4fdb-b555-16ced32d45f8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the overhead resistance, it will suggest that the bulls who are stuck at higher levels are bailing out of their positions. The bears will then try to sink the price to $280.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this negative assumption, if the bulls can push the price above $324.01, the BCH/USD pair could move up to $344.98 and then to $371.70. The gradually rising moving averages and the RSI above 58 suggest that bulls have a minor advantage.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 50-day simple moving average ($12.25) on Nov. 26 and 27 and the bulls have pushed the price back above the overhead resistance at $13.28. The recovery is currently facing resistance at the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $14.4433.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/63e01103-4239-4a60-ba53-534bf5f1a450.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA ($13.40) and the RSI just above the midpoint does not give a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price back below $13.28, it will suggest that sentiment has turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the traders are selling on rallies. A break and close below the 50-day SMA could start a deeper correction.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the bulls push the price above $14.4433, the LINK/USD pair could rally to $15.2994 and then to $16.39. A break above this resistance could resume the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) found support near the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $64.8317 on Nov. 26 and 27. The rebound since then has been sharp but the bulls are currently facing resistance at $88.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6f413d5d-6ece-4ed0-a3b2-105d3eb94c8a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory suggest that bulls have the upper hand. If they can push the price above $88, a retest of $93.9282 will be on the cards. Above this level, the rally could extend to $100.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from the overhead resistance, the LTC/USD pair could remain range-bound for a few days. The pair will turn negative if the bears sink the price below $64.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) surged back above the overhead resistance at $0.155 on Nov. 28, which shows aggressive buying at lower levels. However, the bulls are struggling to sustain the price above $0.17 for the past two days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/5c84d4b1-a2f3-47f0-b3bf-dcc41932826e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This shows that the bears are defending the zone between $0.17 and $0.1826315. If the bears can sink the price below $0.155, a drop to the 20-day EMA ($0.137) is possible.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls buy the dips to $0.155, it will suggest accumulation at this level. A consolidation near the overhead resistance is a positive sign as it shows that traders are not closing their positions in a hurry and are not waiting for deep corrections to buy.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can propel the price above $0.1826315, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair may start its journey to $0.2129 and then to $0.235.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 50-day SMA ($4.52), which shows that the bulls are defending this support. They will now try to push the price above the $5.5899 to $6.0857 resistance zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/8a1bad20-fc14-4024-bab0-09c84772fe6b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the DOT/USD pair could rally to $6.8619 and then to $7.64. The gradually upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 57 suggest that bulls are at a minor advantage.\par \par \uc2 However, if the price again turns down from the overhead resistance zone, the pair could remain stuck in the range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) remains range-bound between $25.6652 and $32. The bounce off the Nov. 26 low suggests that bulls continue to buy near the support of the range. The price has now reached close to the resistance of the range at $32.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6aee6d5d-d22a-4d97-bfb1-83ab1d910e5b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from $32, the BNB/USD pair may extend its stay inside the range. The moving averages are flat but the RSI has jumped into the positive territory, which suggests that the momentum favors the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If the buyers can push the price above $32, the BNB/USD pair could move up to $35.4338. A breakout of this resistance may result in a retest of the all-time high at $39.5941.\par \par \uc2 XLM/USD\par \par \uc2 Stellar Lumens ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM}}}\uc2  ) is facing resistance at the downtrend line but the positive thing is that the bulls have not given up much ground. This shows that the buyers are accumulating on every minor dip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/839d72da-3107-448c-b84e-0c92e5431c3f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XLM/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XLMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above the downtrend line, the XLM/USD pair could rally to $0.231655. The bears may again mount a stiff resistance at this level and if the price turns down from the overhead resistance, a few days of range-bound action is possible.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can drive the price above $0.231655, the next leg of the uptrend could begin. The next target to watch on the upside is $0.2933. Conversely, if the bears sink the price below $0.188, the pair may drop to $0.16.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvZTZiYmQ3N2QtNTBhOS00NjJkLTk1MjgtYTJmZTFiNGY5NzZhLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201130egbu000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Top 5 cryptocurrencies to watch this week: BTC, ETH,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XLM, XEM\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,680 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and a few altcoins have seen aggressive buying at lower levels, which could result in a retest of their recent highs.\par \par \uc2 As Bitcoin price rallied to a new 2020 high, the open interest on CME Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) futures rose to $1.16 billion, making it the world\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cme-overtakes-okex-as-largest-bitcoin-futures-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest}}}\uc2  Bitcoin futures market, according to Arcane Research. This suggests that institutional investors are relatively unmoved by the recent sharp correction in Bitcoin price.\par \par \uc2 Guggenheim Partners\uc2  has become the latest and the largest Wall Street institution that plans to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/guggenheim-partners-prepares-to-dip-investment-fund-s-toes-into-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 invest in Bitcoin}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Guggenheim has sought the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 's (SEC) nod to invest up to 10% of its Macro Opportunities Fund\u8217\'20\'19s net asset value in Bitcoin through the \uc2 Grayscale Bitcoin Trust\uc2 . The fund currently has $5.3 billion in assets, hence, Guggenheim may buy $500 million or more worth of Bitcoin.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/9a41419f-7750-44f6-9a14-9f458b3b7fc4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 The increase in institutional investor\u8217\'20\'19s appetite comes even as Bitcoin is close to its all-time high and this shows they are confident in the long term story of the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Global Macro Investor and Real Vision CEO Raoul Pal said in an interview with Cointelegraph that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s most conservative target is a rally to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-money-may-propel-bitcoin-to-250k-in-one-year-s-time-says-macro-investor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $150,000}}}\uc2  by November 2021. If a large amount of institutional money continues to flow into the crypto space, Bitcoin could even rise to $250,000, added Pal.\par \par \uc2 The long-term fundamentals of cryptocurrencies continue to improve but the price could still fall in the short term and it's likely that investors will view each dip as a buying opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-five cryptocurrencies to find out what opportunities exist.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 In a strong uptrend, the bulls generally buy the dip to the 20-day exponential moving average. The long tails on the Nov. 26 and 27 candlesticks show that bulls aggressively purchased Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/993469fa-edd7-4fe1-9e88-24c9b4773493.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the relative strength index (RSI) in the positive zone suggest that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears will try to stall the current up-move at $18,210.77, which is the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of the most recent fall. If the price turns down from this resistance, a few days of range-bound action is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can push the price above $18,210.77, the BTC/USD pair could rally to $19,459.22 and then to the magical number of $20,000. A breakout of this resistance could start the next leg of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price turns down from the current levels and plummets below $16,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/3013da23-4746-4b2a-b044-389ca5c4f5eb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the rebound off the lower levels has hit a wall near the 50-simple moving average, which is placed just below the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $18,210.77.\par \par \uc2 If the bears can sink the price below $17,500, a retest of $16,400 will be on the cards. If the bulls again buy at lower levels, a few days of range-bound action could ensue.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the bulls can propel the price above $18,210.77, a retest of $19,459.22 is possible.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The long tails on the Nov. 26 and 27 candlesticks show that the bulls purchased the dips in Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) to the breakout level of $488.134 aggressively. This suggests that the sentiment remains positive.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/42e9d281-775d-42e6-83e9-308312b983e4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone suggest that bulls have the upper hand. However, the buyers are unlikely to have an easy path to $625. The bears will try to stall the current rally at the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $569.019.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from this resistance and breaks the 20-day EMA ($512), then a retest of $482 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can push the price above $569.019, the ETH/USD pair could rally to $592.674 and then $622.807. A breakout of this level may start the next leg of the uptrend that could propel the pair to $800.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/ebf673cc-cb61-4ae0-9f13-120c053ed3cd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the bears are defending the 50-SMA. If the price turns down from the current levels and drops below $520, a retest of $482 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can push the price above $569.019, a rally to $592.674 and then to $622.807 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Traders can keep an eye on the RSI because if it sustains above 60, it will suggest that bulls are back in command. On the other hand, if the RSI turns down from 60, it will suggest resistance at higher levels and that could result in a few days of range-bound action.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  had corrected to $0.1199845 on Nov. 26, just above the 78.6% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.1173063. Usually, such a large fall reduces the possibility of the continuation of the uptrend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/a6fb8ff5-5db7-4062-9ebb-461e3a223804.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the long tail on the Nov. 26 candlestick and the sharp rebound on Nov. 28 has again brought the bulls back in contention. The bounce shows that the bull aggressively purchased at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI near the overbought territory suggest that bulls are in command. If the bulls can thrust the price above $0.1826315, the next leg of the uptrend to $0.2129 and then to $0.235 could begin.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the $0.1826315 resistance, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair may remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/511dac32-2726-4e1e-9429-ef1775b2e6da.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages on the 4-hour chart and the RSI in the positive zone show that the bulls have the upper hand. The buyers will now try to drive the price above $0.175 resistance.\par \par \uc2 If they can do that, a retest of $0.1826315 is possible. Conversely, if the price turns down from the overhead resistance, the pair could remain range-bound for a few days. A break below the moving averages will suggest that the bears have made a comeback.\par \par \uc2 XLM/USD\par \par \uc2 The correction in Stellar Lumens ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM}}}\uc2  ), from the recent highs of $0.231655 on Nov. 25, only lasted only for a day on Nov. 26. This suggests that the bulls aggressively purchased the dips as they expect the rally to extend further.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/37d6e443-e98f-4eb8-af57-7e90faa0ea23.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XLM/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XLMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the overbought territory suggest that bulls are in command. The buyers made their intention clear with the 22.83% rally on Nov. 27.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $0.231655, the next leg of the uptrend could begin. The next level to watch on the upside is $0.2933.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears have other plans as they are trying to stall the up-move in the $0.22 to $0.2316555 resistance zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d0ff36ce-a1d4-4370-a19d-7b1570770bf0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XLM/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XLMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to defend the 20-EMA. If the price bounces off this support, the bulls will try to push it above the downtrend line. If they succeed, a retest of $0.231655 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the price below the 20-EMA, the pair could drop to the 50-SMA. If that happens, the pair may consolidate in a large symmetrical triangle for a few days.\par \par \uc2 The advantage will shift in favor of the bears if the pair drops below the $0.145 to $0.140 support zone.\par \par \uc2 XEM/USD\par \par \uc2 NEM ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/nem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XEM}}}\uc2  ) broke out and closed above $0.1690655 on Nov. 25 but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick showed that the bulls booked profits at higher levels. That was followed by a sharp decline on Nov. 26.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/05764603-f9e4-4971-aea9-7fd7269ee0a7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XEM/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XEMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls purchased the dip to the 20-day EMA ($0.147) as seen from the long tail on the Nov. 26 candlestick. The bulls pushed the price back above the overhead resistance on Nov. 27.\par \par \uc2 The price has sustained above $0.1690655 for the past two days but the bulls are facing resistance close to $0.190. The bears are currently attempting to sink the price back below $0.1690655. If they succeed, a drop to the 20-day EMA will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can push the price above the $0.190 to $0.2122 resistance zone, the next leg of the uptrend to $0.275 could begin.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/0a4ec948-e773-4d4b-a839-a4cce8773c25.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XEM/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XEMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the critical support at $0.1690655. If the pair rebounds off this support, the bulls will try to push the price above the downtrend line. If they succeed, the XEM/USD pair could rise to the $0.203 to $0.2122 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the price below $0.1690655, a drop to the 50-SMA is possible. A break below this level could result in a retest of the $0.1428512 support.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvZDJkYjU4NmMtNWE4My00ZmM5LTk4YzgtNjE5MTViYTI3NTg4LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201129egbt000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/27: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOT, XLM, BNB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,831 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s recent correction is healthy, but several altcoins have lost momentum and could remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) rise above $20,000 will have to wait, as the price saw a strong correction and turned away from reaching a new all-time high.\par \par \uc2 Data suggests that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-price-correction-may-not-be-over-on-chain-data-analysts-warn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whales decided to book profits}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-price-correction-may-not-be-over-on-chain-data-analysts-warn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-price-correction-may-not-be-over-on-chain-data-analysts-warn}}}\uc2  when Bitcoin was close to $19,000, and this pulled the price lower. This fall could have resulted in the liquidation of overleveraged positions in the futures market and further aggravated the decline.\par \par \uc2 The current correction {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/stack-funds-hails-bitcoin-s-healthy-correction-predicts-euphoria-ahead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is a healthy sign}}}\uc2 , as the crypto market was becoming overheated as several altcoins rallied vertically in the past week. While some altcoins have given back a large portion of their recent up-move, Bitcoin remains strong, suggesting that investors are buying into support at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/cb965d7f-5593-446b-8193-bfbc636ae25e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Galaxy Digital\uc2  founder and CEO \uc2 Mike Novogratz\uc2  recently said that Bitcoin is attracting institutional investors because it is viewed as a hedge against the debasement of fiat currency. Novogratz suggested investors keep about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/galaxy-digital-ceo-recommends-investing-up-to-3-of-one-s-net-worth-into-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2% to 3% of their net worth}}}\uc2  in Bitcoin with a long-term objective, as he believes BTC will be worth a lot more in five years.\par \par \uc2 However, traders should wait for the price to stabilize and form a base before buying because trying to catch a falling knife could be dangerous. Traders can watch the price action near the critical support levels, then consider buying if they hold steady.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top 10 cryptocurrencies to spot the important support levels that may attract buyers.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) turned down from $19,458.56 on Nov. 25, and the selling intensified on Nov. 26, which pulled the price below the 20-day exponential moving average ($17,048) for the first time since Oct. 8.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/a822bd6e-ca38-4e9f-b09d-0cd4794c6cd9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls defended the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $16,049.61 on Nov. 26, but they are struggling to sustain the price above the 20-day EMA. This suggests that traders are selling on rallies.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $16,049.61, the next support is likely to be the 50% retracement level of $14,996.59, which is placed just above the 50-day simple moving average at $14,535. The bulls are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out, and the relative strength index (RSI) near the midpoint suggests a range formation in the short term.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the stiff overhead resistance at $625 on Nov. 24 as traders booked profits. The selling intensified on Nov. 26, and the biggest altcoin broke below the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $526.348, the 20-day EMA at $504.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/c5c7d0b3-1543-4b4b-a458-46f28dd7daec.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip to the breakout level of $488.134, as seen from the long tail on the Nov. 26 candlestick. However, the bulls are struggling to sustain the rebound as traders are selling on minor rallies.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $488.134, a drop to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $466.755 is possible. A break below this support will shift the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, a strong rebound off the current level or the support at $466.755 will suggest demand at lower levels, and that could keep the ETH/USD pair range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 After the long wick on the Nov. 24 candlestick, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  formed an inside day candlestick pattern on Nov. 25 that closed in the red. This showed that the bulls were booking profits after the sharp rally of the past few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/8ba77e0f-49d7-4cf2-833b-5f1264bc377f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The XRP/USD pair plunged to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.438968 on Nov. 26, but the long tail on the candlestick shows buying at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to give up their advantage. They are selling on rallies and the pair has formed a Doji candlestick pattern today. This suggests that the pair could consolidate in a range for a few days before the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) nosedived on Nov. 25 and 26 and completed a 100% retracement of the latest leg of the uptrend that had started on Nov. 20.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6a0a6fac-6b6f-4265-97d8-f4483449edee.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Although the bulls purchased the dip on Nov. 26, the price turned down from the 20-day EMA ($277) today. This suggests that the sentiment has changed from buy on dips to sell on rallies.\par \par \uc2 The bears will now try to sink the price below the $231 support. If that happens, the BCH/USD pair could drop to $200. Conversely, if the bulls push the price above $280, the pair may rise to $300.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not flip $13.28, the neckline of the inverse head-and-shoulders pattern, into support on Nov. 26. This attracted further selling, and Chainlink's LINK plummeted below the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/8865d593-efa4-46b9-9559-029700c814cf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the 50-day SMA, but the weak rebound off it suggests a lack of urgency to buy, even at these levels.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls fail to push the price back above $13.28 within the next few days, the bears will try to drag the price down to $10. A break below this support could shift the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bulls push and sustain the price above $13.28, it will suggest that the sentiment remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) formed a Doji candlestick pattern on Nov. 24, and that was followed by a sharp drop on Nov. 25. This suggested aggressive profit-booking by the bulls and selling by the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/21957985-114a-42fe-9ec2-6538d266a5c7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The failure of the LTC/USD pair to rebound off the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $75.943, or the 20-day EMA ($73), shows that the bulls are not buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 Although the pair rebounded off the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $64.8317 on Nov. 26, the bulls could not push the price above the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the price breaks below $64, a drop to the 50-day SMA ($60) is possible. Conversely, if the bulls can push the price above the 20-day EMA, it will point to a possible range-bound action for a few days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  formed a dark cloud cover candlestick pattern on Nov. 25, which indicates a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal. This was followed by further selling from the aggressive bears and covering of long positions by the trapped bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/b6f4cac5-1f74-4ba9-b835-4de0cd8e2fdd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair plunged on Nov. 26 and dipped below the 20-day EMA ($0.126), but the long tail on the candlestick shows buying at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 However, the buyers have not been able to sustain the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum, as the bears are selling even on minor rallies. If the bears can sink the price below the 20-day EMA, the pair could drop to $0.1142241.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the pair again rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it could rise to $0.155, then consolidate in a range for a few days before starting the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not sustain the breakout above $5.5899, and Polkadot's DOT plunged back below this level on Nov. 25. This trapped the aggressive bulls who may have been forced to cover their positions in a hurry.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/567c2dc7-8c4c-4485-8253-f2f4f8a546e0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Due to this, and the aggressive selling by the bears, the DOT/USD pair plummeted below the 20-day EMA ($4.91) on Nov. 26. The failure to defend this support is a negative sign and suggests that the bulls are not buying the dips anymore.\par \par \uc2 There was a bounce off the 50-day SMA ($4.46), but the bulls are finding it difficult to sustain the price above the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 50-day SMA, the pair could drop to $3.80, then to the critical support at $3.5321. The flattish moving averages and the RSI just below the midpoint suggest that the pair could remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 XLM/USD\par \par \uc2 Stellar Lumens ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM}}}\uc2  ) formed a Doji candlestick pattern on Nov. 25 that had a long wick. This suggests aggressive selling by the bears at higher levels. The bears continued their selling on the next day, and the altcoin plunged to $0.145377, just above the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.140209.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/47556d95-3222-4df6-91e4-80b5a7688da1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XLM/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XLMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip on Nov. 26 and are currently attempting to resume the uptrend. However, the higher levels are again likely to attract selling.\par \par \uc2 After the large trending moves of the past few days, the \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to reduce, and the XLM/USD pair could consolidate in a range for a few days.\par \par \uc2 This view will be invalidated if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.122) or the bulls propel the price above $0.231655.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not sustain Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) above $33.3888 on Nov. 25, and the price dipped back below the $32 support. This could have trapped several bulls who had purchased on the breakout above the $32\u8211\'20\'13to\u8211\'20\'13$33.3888 zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/2b29e6b6-2f87-41ac-bff3-b15972613727.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Aggressive selling by the bears and liquidation by the bulls on Nov. 26 pulled the price down to $26.35, just above the critical support at $25.6652. If the bears sink the price below this support, the BNB/USD pair could plummet to $19.\par \par \uc2 However, the crisscrossing moving averages and the RSI in the negative territory do not suggest a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears. Therefore, if the price rebounds off $25.6652, the pair may remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvYWI2MGNiNzUtNDE1OC00ZmU4LTk5MDUtNDMwZDBkNDAxYzMyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201127egbr000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/27: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOT, XLM, BNB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,815 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s recent correction is healthy, but several altcoins have lost momentum and could remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) rise above $20,000 will have to wait as the price saw a strong correction which and turned away from reaching a new all-time high.\par \par \uc2 Data suggests that whales decided to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-price-correction-may-not-be-over-on-chain-data-analysts-warn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 book profits}}}\uc2  when Bitcoin was close to $19,000 and this pulled the price lower. This fall could have resulted in the liquidation of overleveraged positions in the futures market and further aggravated the decline.\par \par \uc2 The current {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/stack-funds-hails-bitcoin-s-healthy-correction-predicts-euphoria-ahead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 correction}}}\uc2  is a healthy sign as the crypto market was becoming overheated as several altcoins rallied vertically in the past week. While some altcoins have given back a large portion of their recent up-move, Bitcoin remains strong, suggesting that investors are buying into support at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/cb965d7f-5593-446b-8193-bfbc636ae25e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Galaxy Digital\uc2  founder and CEO \uc2 Mike Novogratz\uc2  recently said that Bitcoin is attracting institutional investors because it is viewed as a hedge against the debasement of fiat currency. Novogratz suggests investors keep about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/galaxy-digital-ceo-recommends-investing-up-to-3-of-one-s-net-worth-into-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2 to 3% of their net worth}}}\uc2  in Bitcoin with a long-term objective as he believes BTC will be worth a lot more in five years.\par \par \uc2 However, traders should wait for the price to stabilize and form a base before buying because trying to catch a falling knife could be dangerous. Traders can watch the price action near the critical support levels and then consider buying if they hold steady.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top-10 cryptocurrencies to spot the important support levels that may attract buyers.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) turned down from $19,458.56 on Nov. 25 and the selling intensified on Nov. 26, which pulled the price below the 20-day exponential moving average ($17,048) for the first time since Oct. 8.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/a822bd6e-ca38-4e9f-b09d-0cd4794c6cd9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls defended the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $16,049.61 on Nov. 26 but they are struggling to sustain the price above the 20-day EMA. This suggests that traders are selling on rallies.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $16,049.61, the next support is likely to be the 50% retracement level of $14,996.59, which is placed just above the 50-day simple moving average at $14,535. The bulls are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the relative strength index (RSI) near the midpoint suggests a range formation in the short term.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the stiff overhead resistance at $625 on Nov. 24 as traders booked profits. The selling intensified on Nov. 26 and the biggest altcoin broke below the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $526.348 and the 20-day EMA at $504.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/c5c7d0b3-1543-4b4b-a458-46f28dd7daec.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip to the breakout level of $488.134 as seen from the long tail on Nov. 26 candlestick. However, the bulls are struggling to sustain the rebound as traders are selling on minor rallies.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $488.134, a drop to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $466.755 is possible. A break below this support will shift the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, a strong rebound off the current level or the support at $466.755 will suggest demand at lower levels and that could keep the ETH/USD pair range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 After the long wick on the Nov. 24 candlestick, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  formed an inside day candlestick pattern on Nov. 25 that closed in the red. This showed that the bulls were booking profits after the sharp rally of the past few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/8ba77e0f-49d7-4cf2-833b-5f1264bc377f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The XRP/USD pair plunged to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.438968 on Nov. 26 but the long tail on the candlestick shows buying at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to give up their advantage. They are selling on rallies and the pair has formed a Doji candlestick pattern today. This suggests that the pair could consolidate in a range for a few days before the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) nosedived on Nov. 25 and 26 and completed a 100% retracement of the latest leg of the uptrend that had started on Nov. 20.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6a0a6fac-6b6f-4265-97d8-f4483449edee.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Although the bulls purchased the dip on Nov. 26, the price turned down from the 20-day EMA ($277) today. This suggests that the sentiment has changed from buy on dips to sell on rallies.\par \par \uc2 The bears will now try to sink the price below the $231 support. If that happens, the BCH/USD pair could drop to $200. Conversely, if the bulls push the price above $280, the pair may rise to $300.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not flip $13.28, the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders pattern, into support on Nov. 26. This attracted further selling and Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) plummeted below the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/8865d593-efa4-46b9-9559-029700c814cf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the 50-day SMA but the weak rebound off it suggests a lack of urgency to buy even at these levels.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls fail to push the price back above $13.28 within the next few days, the bears will try to drag the price down to $10. A break below this support could shift the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bulls push and sustain the price above $13.28, it will suggest that the sentiment remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) formed a Doji candlestick pattern on Nov. 24 and that was followed by a sharp drop on Nov. 25. This suggested aggressive profit booking by the bulls and selling by the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/21957985-114a-42fe-9ec2-6538d266a5c7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The failure of the LTC/USD pair to rebound off the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $75.943, or the 20-day EMA ($73) shows that the bulls are not buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 Although the pair rebounded off the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $64.8317 on Nov. 26, the bulls could not push the price above the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the price breaks below $64, a drop to the 50-day SMA ($60) is possible. Conversely, if the bulls can push the price above the 20-day EMA, it will point to a possible range-bound action for a few days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) formed a dark cloud cover candlestick pattern on Nov. 25, which indicates a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal. This was followed by further selling from the aggressive bears and covering of long positions by the trapped bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/b6f4cac5-1f74-4ba9-b835-4de0cd8e2fdd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair plunged on Nov. 26 and dipped below the 20-day EMA ($0.126) but the long tail on the candlestick shows buying at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 However, the buyers have not been able to sustain the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum as the bears are selling even on minor rallies. If the bears can sink the price below the 20-day EMA, the pair could drop to $0.1142241.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the pair again rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it could rise to $0.155 and then consolidate in a range for a few days before starting the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not sustain the breakout above $5.5899 and Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) plunged back below this level on Nov. 25. This trapped the aggressive bulls who may have been forced to cover their positions in a hurry.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/567c2dc7-8c4c-4485-8253-f2f4f8a546e0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Due to this, and the aggressive selling by the bears, the DOT/USD pair plummeted below the 20-day EMA ($4.91) on Nov. 26. The failure to defend this support is a negative sign and suggests that the bulls are not buying the dips anymore.\par \par \uc2 There was a bounce off the 50-day SMA ($4.46) but the bulls are finding it difficult to sustain the price above the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 50-day SMA, the pair could drop to $3.80 and then to the critical support at $3.5321. The flattish moving averages and the RSI just below the midpoint suggest that the pair could remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 XLM/USD\par \par \uc2 Stellar Lumens ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM}}}\uc2  ) formed a Doji candlestick pattern on Nov. 25 that had a long wick. This suggests aggressive selling by the bears at higher levels. The bears continued their selling on the next day and the altcoin plunged to $0.145377, just above the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.140209.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/47556d95-3222-4df6-91e4-80b5a7688da1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XLM/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XLMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip on Nov. 26 and are currently attempting to resume the uptrend. However, the higher levels are again likely to attract selling.\par \par \uc2 After the large trending moves of the past few days, the \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to reduce and the XLM/USD pair could consolidate in a range for a few days.\par \par \uc2 This view will be invalidated if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.122) or the bulls propel the price above $0.231655.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not sustain Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) above $33.3888 on Nov. 25 and the price dipped back below the $32 support. This could have trapped several bulls who had purchased on the breakout above the $32 to $33.3888 zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/2b29e6b6-2f87-41ac-bff3-b15972613727.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Aggressive selling by the bears and liquidation by the bulls on Nov. 26 pulled the price down to $26.35, just above the critical support at $25.6652. If the bears sink the price below this support, the BNB/USD pair could plummet to $19.\par \par \uc2 However, the crisscrossing moving averages and the RSI in the negative territory do not suggest a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears. Therefore, if the price rebounds off $25.6652, the pair may remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvYWI2MGNiNzUtNDE1OC00ZmU4LTk5MDUtNDMwZDBkNDAxYzMyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201127egbr000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/25: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOT, BNB, XLM\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,916 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Traders seem to be hesitant to continue their purchases after the recent Bitcoin price rally\par \par \uc2 The crypto market has been in a strong bull run over the past few days, and that has pushed Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) to its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-has-now-only-been-higher-one-day-in-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-has-now-only-been-higher-one-day-in-history}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-has-now-only-been-higher-one-day-in-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second-best day ever}}}\uc2 . Almost every trader now seems to be fixated on the magical figure of $20,000 per BTC.\par \par \uc2 After such a sharp up-move, some traders are calling for a top, while others are projecting lofty targets for the future.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/1e3e62a4-acd1-4796-9cb6-8d003eb17d2f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency market daily performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 CNBC Fast Money host Brian Kelly, for example, believes that the recent volitile moves in altcoins, overpriced Bitcoin address growth, and rising funding rates pointing to the arrival of retail traders may be a warning sign of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/2-counterarguments-for-cnbc-s-brian-kelly-who-sees-a-19k-bitcoin-top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 short to medium-term top}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/2-counterarguments-for-cnbc-s-brian-kelly-who-sees-a-19k-bitcoin-top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/2-counterarguments-for-cnbc-s-brian-kelly-who-sees-a-19k-bitcoin-top}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the other end of the spectrum are analysts such as Off the Chain Capital chief investment officer Brian Estes who believes that Bitcoin could rally to $100,000 in one year, and even better, to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/no-debate-that-bitcoin-will-increase-20x-says-gold-industry-insider"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/no-debate-that-bitcoin-will-increase-20x-says-gold-industry-insider}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/no-debate-that-bitcoin-will-increase-20x-says-gold-industry-insider"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $288,000 by the end of 2021}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Another \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view was projected by Gold Bullion International co-founder Dan Tapiero, who opined that Bitcoin could rally to \u8220\'20\'1Csomewhere between $300,000 and $500,000\u8221\'20\'1D in the next five years.\par \par \uc2 During a bull cycle, it is very easy to get sucked into making hasty decisions. Actions taken due to greed could wipe out the trading account, especially if traders use excessive leverage in a volatile market. Therefore, traders should stick to their trading strategies and mitigate risk.\par \par \uc2 After the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/these-5-altcoins-are-beating-every-major-cryptocurrency-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vertical rallies of the past few days}}}\uc2 , is there more steam left, or is it time for a correction? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) broke the $19,000 barrier on Nov. 24 and is trying to inch higher toward the $20,000 mark. The formation of a Doji candlestick pattern today suggests hesitation among the bulls to buy aggressively at the current levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/58d2e13c-b246-45ab-ac34-3d6bbb149318.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the positive thing is that the bulls have not allowed the price to correct, even to the 20-day exponential moving average ($17,095), since the uptrend started on Oct. 8. This shows that the bulls are buying on every minor dip.\par \par \uc2 Due to this incessant buying, the relative strength index (RSI) has remained in the overbought zone since Oct 21. The bears may try to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-faces-this-final-resistance-zone-before-20k-all-time-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stall the rally before the $20,000}}}\uc2  level, but unless they sink the price below the 20-day EMA, the bulls remain in control.\par \par \uc2 If the BTC/USD pair rises above $20,000 without a meaningful correction, then it may continue vertically, before turning around sharply. In a market with strong \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum, it is foolhardy to call a top.\par \par \uc2 The frenzied buying usually signals a top, but before the reversal happens, it also offers the best periods to make money to the prudent trader.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, traders can book partial profits at stiff resistances and protect their remaining positions with a trailing stop-loss order to protect their paper profits.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) is facing profit-booking near the stiff overhead resistance at $625. However, the shallow correction shows that the bulls are not closing their positions in a hurry. The bulls may again attempt to push the price above $625 in the next few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/0d739651-b303-41f5-9491-c69ac8e0f3cd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the ETH/USD pair could start its journey to the next major resistance at $800. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the overbought zone suggest that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 However, if the ETH/USD pair turns down from the overhead resistance, the bears may sink the pair to the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level at $526.348, and a deeper correction could extend the decline to the 50% retracement level at $496.552.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  price soared to an intraday high at $0.780574 on Nov. 24 from a low of $0.227813 on Nov. 3, which is a 242% rally within a short time. Such vertical rallies are not sustainable. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/xrp-price-spikes-to-0-90-crashes-in-seconds-as-coinbase-goes-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long wick on the Nov. 24 candlestick}}}\uc2  shows profit-booking at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7ff6daf7-e597-4cef-ad1c-0f1659c384e6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The RSI above 91 suggests that the markets are overheated in the short term and need to cool off. However, the long tail on today\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows that bulls continue to buy at lower levels in anticipation of a further up-move.\par \par \uc2 If the XRP/USD pair rallies above $0.780574, the uptrend could enter a blow-off phase and reach $0.96. However, if the price turns down from the overhead resistance, the pair may remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) rallied hard on Nov. 23 and 24 and broke above the $353 resistance, but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels. The long wick on the Nov. 24 candlestick shows profit-booking at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d3c709fb-20e9-4562-a10d-aee6904245c0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls again pushed the price above $353 today but are finding it difficult to sustain the higher levels. This could start a correction to the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level at $324.13, then to the 50% retracement level at $309.44.\par \par \uc2 A shallow correction will suggest that traders are not booking profits aggressively and fresh buyers are not waiting for a large correction to get in. That will increase the possibility of a resumption of the uptrend to $420, then to $500.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  has been sustaining above the neckline of the inverse head-and-shoulders pattern for the past few days but has failed to pick up momentum. This increases the possibility of a retest of the breakout level at $13.28.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d1255d85-f902-4c74-a810-9ed6d051b34e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A strong rebound off $13.28 will flip it to support and could start the next leg of the up-move, which may take the LINK/USD pair to $18, then to $19.2731. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory suggest bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears sink the price below $13.28. Such a move would suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap. A break below the 50-day simple moving average ($11.96) will tilt the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) once again closed above $84.3374 on Nov. 23. However, the Doji candlestick pattern on Nov. 24 shows indecision among the bulls and the bears. This indecision has resolved to the downside today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/9369179f-af53-4f68-8c27-b8f6ac161490.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears are currently attempting to sink the price back below the breakout level of $84.3374. If they succeed, the LTC/USD pair could drop to the 20-day EMA ($74).\par \par \uc2 If the pair rebounds strongly off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will once again attempt to resume the uptrend by pushing the price above $93.9282. If they manage to do that, a retest of $100 will be in the cards.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, a break below the 20-day EMA would suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has weakened.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged above the $0.155 resistance on Nov. 24 and hit an intraday high at $0.1826315. However, the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows profit-booking by traders at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/ee46b777-fdba-4fea-8a89-78e5952349f4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears attempted to pull the price back below the breakout level at $0.155 today, but the long tail on the candlestick shows traders are buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair has formed an inside day candlestick pattern today, which suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears. This could result in a consolidation for a few days before the next trending move starts.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can propel the price above $0.20, the pair may rally to $0.24, then to $0.28. If both these levels are crossed, the rally could extend to $0.40. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price dips and sustains below $0.155.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are having a tough time sustaining Polkadot's DOT above the $5.5899 level. Although the bulls pushed the price to $6.0857 on Nov. 24, they could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/cd70c8cf-11ed-413d-ae36-074dbeb48940.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears are currently attempting to sink and sustain the price back below $5.5899. If they succeed, the DOT/USD pair could drop to the 20-day EMA ($4.98).\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off this level, the bulls will once again try to push the price above $6.0857. If they succeed, a rally to $6.8619 will be on the cards. The upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive territory give the advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, the pair could spend some more time inside the range.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke above the $32\u8211\'20\'13$33.3888 resistance zone on Nov. 24, but the bulls are struggling to build upon this strength. The bears are currently attempting to pull the price back below $32.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/13c640a2-77c1-47b1-b0d1-c721364e7ebd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off $32, the BNB/USD pair could resume its up-move towards the target objective of $38.3348, which is just below the all-time high at $39.5941.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears succeed in sinking the price back below $32, it may catch off guard the aggressive bulls who have purchased the breakout. If the price sustains below $32, the pair may remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 XLM/USD\par \par \uc2 Stellar Lumen ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM}}}\uc2  ) has surged from $0.083684 on Nov. 20 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/stellar-lumens-doubles-in-price-following-upgrade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to an intraday high of $0.231655 today}}}\uc2 , a 176% gain within a short time. The next resistance on the upside is $0.2864.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/07e48953-4cee-4bf6-9fc5-3248d78c256f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XLM/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XLMUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The sharp rally of the past few days has pushed the RSI above the 92 level. Usually, such deeply overbought levels are not sustainable, and traders can expect a correction to start in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 A vertical rally is usually followed by a sharp correction. The first support on the downside is the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.17513. The bulls are likely to buy this dip aggressively, and the XLM/USD pair could remain volatile for the next few days.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvNmY0OTBhYzUtZDk3NC00NGIwLTkzNjktNGY2ZmI1YmU0NjdkLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201125egbp000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 These 5 altcoins are beating every major cryptocurrency this week\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 503 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 XRP, Stellar, IOTA and Cardano are the standouts this week in returns as traders herald "altseason"\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has topped $19,000 in a fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  surge, but traders are all about altcoins on Nov. 24.\par \par \uc2 In what many are heralding as the beginning of \u8220\'20\'1Calt season,\u8221\'20\'1D large-cap cryptocurrencies are seeing their biggest gains in three years.\par \par \uc2 XRP, XLM lead new \u8220\'20\'1Calt season\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph takes a look at five of the biggest movers, all of which have returned to at least a $1 billion market cap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/36cba605-83f9-4335-9673-42e9c62d2c10.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Top altcoins by weekly gains. Source: CoinMarketCap\par \par \uc2 XRP\par \par \uc2 Ripple\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  token is gaining traction on social media after a curious lull, thanks to its weekly gains that have topped 110%.\par \par \uc2 At press time, XRP/USD traded at $0.62, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/xrp-price-spikes-to-0-90-crashes-in-seconds-as-coinbase-goes-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 having reached $0.92 before a sudden 30% crash}}}\uc2 , which came in tandem with \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  experiencing a major technical outage.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the token still remains far from its peak of over $3, or roughly 80% from its all-time high.\par \par \uc2 By comparison, Bitcoin is now just 3% from its all-time high in December 2017.\par \par \uc2 Stellar Lumen (XLM)\par \par \uc2 On the back of XRP\u8217\'20\'19s resurgence, Stellar Lumen ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM}}}\uc2  ) beat its daily gains to pass $0.18 and deliver over 90% weekly returns.\par \par \uc2 A classic move for the sister altcoin, which tends to follow XRP in bull markets, Lumen returned to its position from November 2018. Its all-time highs lie at just above $0.60.\par \par \uc2 Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Another major success story this week, Cardano's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  topped 50% weekly gains, much of which occurred prior to Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s altcoin action.\par \par \uc2 With a market cap now above $5 billion, Cardano became the eighth-largest cryptocurrency, clipping $0.16.\par \par \uc2 Against a backdrop of all-time highs above $1, however, much ground remains for investors to see significant returns from previous years.\par \par \uc2 IOTA (MIOTA)\par \par \uc2 The fourth-biggest weekly rises belonged to Iota ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/iota-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MIOTA}}}\uc2  ) on Wednesday, whose weekly gains totalled just under 50%.\par \par \uc2 Currently at 26th on CoinMarketCap\u8217\'20\'19s list of cryptocurrencies, Iota hit $0.36 this week, but the path to new all-time highs remains decidedly uncertain \u8212\'20\'14 those lie at close to $5.50.\par \par \uc2 Dash\par \par \uc2 A familiar face among altcoin traders, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/dash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dash}}}\uc2  brought up the rear among the week\u8217\'20\'19s risers, with Dash/USD gaining nearly 40% over the past seven days.\par \par \uc2 At press time, the pair traded at $115, still far from its record of near $1,500.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/499910bb-018d-4627-bc24-e42dd032eb5f.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency market cap historical chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin dominance. In case you were wondering, this is what alt season looks like,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/scottmelker/status/1331200681848475650"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  popular trader Scott Melker, noting that the index failed to break upward this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CQuite reminiscent of 2017. Alts have a brief window to party, then you get back into Bitcoin, it rages. Rinse, repeat,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur week of alt euphoria was amazing. Now we wait and see.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvY2M4N2IwNDItNDkyZC00N2RmLTg5NmEtOTU0N2YzZTUyZGE3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201124egbo000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 These 5 altcoins are beating every major cryptocurrency this week\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 501 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 XRP, Stellar, IOTA and Cardano are the standouts this week in returns as traders herald "altseason"\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has topped $19,000 in a fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  surge, but traders are all about altcoins on Nov. 24.\par \par \uc2 In what many are heralding as the beginning of \u8220\'20\'1Caltseason,\u8221\'20\'1D large-cap cryptocurrencies are seeing their biggest gains in three years.\par \par \uc2 XRP, XLM lead new \u8220\'20\'1Caltseason\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph takes a look at five of the biggest movers, all of which have returned to at least a $1 billion market cap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldins