\par \uc2 WIth a market cap now above $5 billion, Cardano became the eighth largest cryptocurrency, clipping $0.16.\par \par \uc2 Against a backdrop of all-time highs above $1, however, much ground remains for investors to see significant returns from previous years.\par \par \uc2 IOTA (MIOTA)\par \par \uc2 The fourth-biggest weekly rises belonged to IOTA ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/iota-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MIOTA}}}\uc2  ) on Wednesday, weekly gains for which totalled just under 50%.\par \par \uc2 Currently at 26th on CoinMarketCap\u8217\'20\'19s list of cryptocurrencies, IOTA hit $0.36 this week, but the path to new all-time highs remains decidedly uncertain \u8212\'20\'14 those lie at close to $5.50.\par \par \uc2 Dash (DASH)\par \par \uc2 A familiar face among altcoin traders, Dash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/dash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DASH}}}\uc2  ), brought up the rear among the week\u8217\'20\'19s risers, with DASH/USD gaining nearly 40% over the past 7 days.\par \par \uc2 At press time, the pair traded at $115, still far from its record of near $1,500.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/499910bb-018d-4627-bc24-e42dd032eb5f.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency market cap historical chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin dominance. In case you were wondering, this is what alt season looks like,\u8221\'20\'1D said popular trader {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/scottmelker/status/1331200681848475650"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scott Melker}}}\uc2 , noting that the index failed to break upward this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CQuite reminiscent of 2017. Alts have a brief window to party, then you get back into Bitcoin, it rages. Rinse, repeat,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur week of alt euphoria was amazing. Now we wait and see.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvY2M4N2IwNDItNDkyZC00N2RmLTg5NmEtOTU0N2YzZTUyZGE3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201124egbo0008f\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/23: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, LTC, BCH, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,809 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin could consolidate for a few more days as the action shifts to Ether, XRP, and other large-cap altcoins.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has been leading the current crypto rally for the past few weeks, and this has boosted its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/charts/#dominance-percentage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dominance}}}\uc2  from 56% on Sep. 3 to 67% on Nov. 18. However, as Bitcoin nears its all-time high, it seems to be losing momentum as the action shifts to altcoins. This has pulled Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s dominance down to about 62.3%.\par \par \uc2 No long-term bull market can be led by one leader alone. There are periodic rotations when the leader enters a consolidation or a minor correction while others take the lead. A similar rotation is currently playing out in the crypto markets, with Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  leading the rally while Bitcoin digests its gains.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/35706c5b-891a-4396-943d-42dc830e0185.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 As the current bull phase matures and the commentary turns even more \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , several traders who have missed a large part of the move may start buying the underperforming assets that were not swept up in the bull run.\par \par \uc2 This phase usually marks a top. Hence, traders can keep a watch on the underperforming coins. When they start flying, it could be a sign that it\u8217\'20\'19s time to book profits and run with your money.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top 10 cryptocurrencies to determine whether the uptrend will continue or if a short-term correction around the corner.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is currently witnessing a minor correction in a strong uptrend. Usually, the pullback in a strong trend lasts between one to three days before the trend resumes.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/eac06808-d3c5-4840-8fe8-c42a60b39fcb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 As the bulls have not given up much ground from the 52-week high at $18,965.75, it suggests that traders are not hurrying to close their positions because they expect the uptrend to continue.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the relative strength index (RSI) in the overbought territory suggest that bulls are in command. A breakout above $18,965.75 could result in a rally to $20,000, which may act as a psychological resistance.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can drive the price above $20,000, the BTC/USD pair will enter uncharted territory and may rally vertically. Usually, after such a phase, a sharp correction is expected.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price turns down from the current levels and the bears sink the pair below the 20-day exponential moving average at $16,657.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether picked up momentum after the bulls pushed the price above $488.134 on Nov. 20. Although the bears attempted to stall the rally on Nov. 22, the bulls purchased the dips aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/48ba97ab-e717-46dd-a3de-6989bc233880.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up, and the RSI is close to 80, which suggests that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 The uptrend has resumed today with a breakout of the psychological $600 level. The next resistance is at $625, but if the bulls can thrust the price above this level, the ETH/USD pair could rally to $800.\par \par \uc2 However, after the sharp run of the past few days, the pair may stall at $625 and digest the gains for a few days before starting the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 XRP seems to be in an urgency to make up for the underperformance during the current crypto bull run. After the Doji candlestick on Nov. 22, the bulls have asserted their dominance today and have pushed the price above the $0.50 resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/693c1c59-c597-46b1-ab5c-e98fa41bd14a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 There is a minor resistance at $0.60 but if the bulls can drive the price above it, the XRP/USD pair could rally to $0.78.\par \par \uc2 While overbought levels on the RSI is a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sign during the early stages of an uptrend, a reading above 90 suggests panic buying. Usually, such periods of frenzied buying are followed by a sharp correction or a consolidation.\par \par \uc2 A break below the intraday low of Nov. 22 at $0.40 could intensify selling and signal an end to the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  is currently in an uptrend. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory suggest that the bulls are in command. The pattern target of the breakout of the inverse head-and-shoulders setup is $19.2731.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7a8d204b-312e-43c2-ad85-7d2843740b58.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are likely to have other plans. They will try to stall the up-move and pull the price back below the breakout level of $13.28. The trend will tilt in favor of the bears if they can sink and sustain the price below $11.80.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the LINK/USD pair rebounds off $13.28, it will suggest demand at lower levels. The bulls will then attempt to resume the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 There is a tough battle in progress near the $84.3374 level. The bulls are attempting to sustain \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) above this level, while the bears are attempting to drag the price below it.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/771fcebc-319a-48c8-b500-ad2cc71c810c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The long tail on the Nov. 22 candlestick shows strong buying at lower levels, while the long wick on today\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows selling at higher levels. This could keep the LTC/USD pair range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the overbought zone suggest bulls are in control. If they can push the price above $90, the next leg of the uptrend to $100 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears can sink the price below $78, the pair may drop to the 20-day EMA ($71). Such a move will suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) soared above the overhead resistance at $280 on Nov. 21. Although the bears tried to fake this up-move by pulling the price back below $280 on Nov. 22, they could not sustain the lower levels. This suggests that bulls are buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/261645b9-85f8-4db9-be54-3ade7d57a95b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $312.52, the BCH/USD pair could rally to $338, then to $353. The bears may mount a strong defense in this zone, but if the bulls can overcome this hurdle, the momentum could pick up.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up, and the RSI is in the positive territory, which suggests that the buyers are in control. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears sink and sustain the price below $280.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot's DOT broke above the stiff overhead resistance at $5.5899 on Nov. 21. However, the bears pulled the price back below $5.5899 on Nov. 22 but could not sustain the lower levels. This suggests that the bulls are buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/c567030c-8f54-438c-8d07-86c3fa5a6ba3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are again attempting to start a new uptrend by pushing the price above the overhead resistance at $5.8453. If they succeed, the DOT/USD pair could rally to $6.8619.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA ($4.81) and the RSI near the overbought zone suggest an advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the bears pull the price back below $5.5899 and then sink the pair below $4.95. Such a move will suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke and closed above the $0.1142241 resistance on Nov. 20. This attracted aggressive buying from the bulls, who easily pushed the price above the overhead resistances.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/eaad1a96-bed6-4433-9496-d81fd79f4625.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair had risen to a new 52-week high today, but the bears are trying to stall the current uptrend at the $0.1550 resistance. During the three previous occasions, when the RSI had risen close to 80, the pair had consolidated for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Hence, a few days of range-bound action near the $0.1550 overhead resistance is possible. If the bulls can drive the price above $0.1550, the rally could extend to $0.20. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair plummets from the current levels and closes below $0.128.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke out and closed above the $27.30\u8211\'20\'13$28.97 range on Nov. 21, but the bulls could not capitalize on this strength to push the price to $32. This attracted selling by the bears, and they tried to pull the price back below $28.97 on Nov. 22 but failed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/0fe14032-f69c-497e-b4a5-79cfaa7da751.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are again attempting to push the price toward the top of the $25.6652\u8211\'20\'13$32 range. If the price turns down from the overhead resistance at $32, it will suggest a lack of demand at higher levels and a few more days of range-bound action is likely.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the bulls can propel the price above the $32\u8211\'20\'13$33.3888 resistance zone, the BNB/USD pair could start the next leg of the journey that may carry it to the all-time high at $39.5941.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) surged above the $181 overhead resistance on Nov. 21, which marked a breakout from the $146\u8211\'20\'13$181 range the price had been stuck in since early September. After the breakout from a range, the bears usually try to fake the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  move, and they tried doing it on Nov. 22.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f551d638-f2de-4f6c-bde6-16c9c50e104a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls used the lower levels to buy, and they have currently resumed the new up-move that can reach $227, and if this level is also scaled, the rally may extend to $258.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price again turns down from the current level, the BSV/USD pair could remain range-bound between $181 and $194.\par \par \uc2 The trend will tilt in favor of the bears if they can sink and sustain the price below $181. Such a move could catch the aggressive bulls off guard and result in a drop to the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvNjExNmNkYzAtM2M4Yi00YTFhLWJlM2EtM2FkYWM3NzVhZmE0LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201123egbn000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/23: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, LTC, BCH, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,814 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin could consolidate for a few more days as the action shifts to Ether, XRP, and other large-cap altcoins.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has been leading the current crypto rally for the past few weeks and this has boosted its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/charts/#dominance-percentage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dominance}}}\uc2  from 56% on Sep. 3 to 67% on Nov. 18. However, as Bitcoin nears its all-time high, it seems to be losing momentum as the action shifts to the altcoins. This has pulled Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s dominance down to about 62.3%.\par \par \uc2 No long-term bull market can be led by one leader alone. There are periodic rotations when the leader enters a consolidation or a minor correction, while others take the lead. A similar rotation is currently playing out in the crypto markets, with Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  leading the rally while Bitcoin digests its gains.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/35706c5b-891a-4396-943d-42dc830e0185.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 As the current bull phase matures and the commentary turns even more \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , several traders who have missed a large part of the move may start buying the underperforming assets which were not swept up in the bull run.\par \par \uc2 This phase usually marks a top. Hence, traders can keep a watch on the underperforming coins. When they start flying, it could be a sign that it\u8217\'20\'19s time to book profits and run with your money.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top-10 cryptocurrencies to determine whether the uptrend will continue or if a short-term correction around the corner.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) is currently witnessing a minor correction in a strong uptrend. Usually, the pullback in a strong trend lasts between one to three days before the trend resumes.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/eac06808-d3c5-4840-8fe8-c42a60b39fcb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 As the bulls have not given up much ground from the 52-week high at $18,965.75, it suggests that traders are not hurrying to close their positions because they expect the uptrend to continue.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the relative strength index (RSI) in the overbought territory suggest that bulls are in command. A breakout above $18,965.75 could result in a rally to $20,000, which may act as a psychological resistance.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can drive the price above $20,000, the BTC/USD pair will enter uncharted territory and may rally vertically. Usually, after such a phase, a sharp correction could be expected.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price turns down from the current levels and the bears sink the pair below the 20-day exponential moving average at $16,657.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) picked up momentum after the bulls pushed the price above $488.134 on Nov. 20. Although the bears attempted to stall the rally on Nov. 22, the bulls purchased the dips aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/48ba97ab-e717-46dd-a3de-6989bc233880.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is close to 80, which suggests that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 The uptrend has resumed today with a breakout of the psychological $600 level. The next resistance is at $625 but if the bulls can thrust the price above this level, the ETH/USD pair could rally to $800.\par \par \uc2 However, after the sharp run of the past few days, the pair may stall at $625 and digest the gains for a few days before starting the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  seems to be in an urgency to make up for the underperformance during the current crypto bull run. After the Doji candlestick on Nov. 22, the bulls have asserted their dominance today and have pushed the price above the $0.50 resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/693c1c59-c597-46b1-ab5c-e98fa41bd14a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 There is a minor resistance at $0.60 but if the bulls can drive the price above it, the XRP/USD pair could rally to $0.78.\par \par \uc2 While overbought levels on the RSI is a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sign during the early stages of an uptrend, a reading above 90 suggests panic buying. Usually, such periods of frenzied buying are followed by a sharp correction or a consolidation.\par \par \uc2 A break below the intraday low of Nov. 22 at $0.40 could intensify selling and signal an end to the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) is currently in an uptrend. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory suggest that bulls are in command. The pattern target of the breakout of the inverse head and shoulders setup is $19.2731.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7a8d204b-312e-43c2-ad85-7d2843740b58.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are likely to have other plans. They will try to stall the up-move and pull the price back below the breakout level of $13.28. The trend will tilt in favor of the bears if they can sink and sustain the price below $11.80.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the LINK/USD pair rebounds off $13.28, it will suggest demand at lower levels. The bulls will then attempt to resume the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 There is a tough battle in progress near the $84.3374 level. The bulls are attempting to sustain \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) above this level while the bears are attempting to drag the price below it.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/771fcebc-319a-48c8-b500-ad2cc71c810c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The long tail on the Nov. 22 candlestick shows strong buying at lower levels while the long wick on today\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows selling at higher levels. This could keep the LTC/USD pair range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the overbought zone suggest bulls are in control. If they can push the price above $90, the next leg of the uptrend to 