om/uploads/2020-11/c567030c-8f54-438c-8d07-86c3fa5a6ba3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are again attempting to start a new uptrend by pushing the price above the overhead resistance at $5.8453. If they succeed, the DOT/USD pair could rally to $6.8619.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA ($4.81) and the RSI near the overbought zone suggest an advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the bears pull the price back below $5.5899 and then sink the pair below $4.95. Such a move will suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the $0.1142241 resistance on Nov. 20. This attracted aggressive buying from the bulls who easily pushed the price above the overhead resistances.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/eaad1a96-bed6-4433-9496-d81fd79f4625.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair had risen to a new 52-week high today but the bears are trying to stall the current uptrend at the $0.1550 resistance. During the three previous occasions, when the RSI had risen close to 80, the pair had consolidated for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Hence, a few days of range-bound action near the $0.1550 overhead resistance is possible. If the bulls can drive the price above $0.1550, the rally could extend to $0.20. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair plummets from the current levels and closes below $0.128.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke out and closed above the $27.30 to $28.97 range on Nov. 21 but the bulls could not capitalize on this strength and push the price to $32. This attracted selling by the bears and they tried to pull the price back below $28.97 on Nov. 22 but failed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/0fe14032-f69c-497e-b4a5-79cfaa7da751.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are again attempting to push the price towards the top of the $25.6652 to $32 range. If the price turns down from the overhead resistance at $32, it will suggest a lack of demand at higher levels and a few more days of range-bound action is likely.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the bulls can propel the price above the $32 to $33.3888 resistance zone, the BNB/USD pair could start the next leg of the journey that may carry it to the all-time high at $39.5941.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) surged above the $181 overhead resistance on Nov. 21, which marked a breakout from the $146 to $181 range the price had been stuck in since early September. After the breakout from a range, the bears usually try to fake the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  move and they tried doing it on Nov. 22.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f551d638-f2de-4f6c-bde6-16c9c50e104a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls used the lower levels to buy and they have currently resumed the new up-move that can reach $227 and if this level is also scaled, the rally may extend to $258.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price again turns down from the current level, the BSV/USD pair could remain range-bound between $181 and $194.\par \par \uc2 The trend will tilt in favor of the bears if they can sink and sustain the price below $181. Such a move could catch the aggressive bulls off guard and result in a drop to the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvNjExNmNkYzAtM2M4Yi00YTFhLWJlM2EtM2FkYWM3NzVhZmE0LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201123egbn000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/20: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, LTC, BCH, DOT, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,907 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price is back on the path to a new all-time high and it seems altcoins intend to follow suit.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) current rally has largely been led by investments from institutional investors and publicly listed companies. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/corporate-bitcoin-frenzy-companies-now-hold-15-3-billion-in-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Data from Bitcointreasuries shows}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/corporate-bitcoin-frenzy-companies-now-hold-15-3-billion-in-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/corporate-bitcoin-frenzy-companies-now-hold-15-3-billion-in-btc}}}\uc2  that companies hold about 4.54% of the current Bitcoin supply.\par \par \uc2 A survey of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/survey-of-millionaires-finds-73-own-or-want-to-invest-in-crypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 700 high-net-worth}}}\uc2  individuals chosen from across the globe shows that about 73% of respondents either own or want to own cryptocurrencies before the end of 2022. The proposed influx of money from large investors could boost demand and drive crypto prices higher.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/07c3d68d-e3bd-4723-ac64-43b61b38b4fe.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg Intelligence strategist Mike McGlone believes that if history repeats itself, Bitcoin could rally to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bloomberg-s-mcglone-thinks-bitcoin-could-hit-170k-over-the-next-two-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $170,000}}}\uc2  over the next two years. McGlone pointed out that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus gold was the lowest on record, and while \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in risky assets across the globe has been increasing, Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been in decline. However, in the short term, McGlone expects Bitcoin to consolidate before zooming higher.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/corporate-bitcoin-frenzy-companies-now-hold-15-3-billion-in-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with Cointelegraph}}}\uc2 , Nugget\u8217\'20\'19s News CEO Alex Saunders said that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price could rally to \u8220\'20\'1C$100,000 in the next five years,\u8221\'20\'1D and if it becomes the global reserve currency, then it could reach $1 million by 2035.\par \par \uc2 When markets are \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is easy to get sucked into the rally due to greed. However, every bull phase witnesses periodic corrections; hence, traders should be careful and protect their paper profits with a suitable stop loss.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top 10 cryptocurrencies to spot the critical resistance and support levels to watch over the coming days.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s correction from $18,466.14 was short-lived, as the bulls defended the $17,200 support and have currently pushed the price to a new 52-week high. This suggests that the uptrend is strong and the bulls are firmly in control.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/ded8797f-aab4-42ff-9bd3-b029b4cffc04.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The next resistance on the upside is the all-time high at $19,531.90, then the psychological level at $20,000. If the bulls can propel the price above $20,000 in the current leg of the uptrend, the momentum could further pick up and make a blow-off top.\par \par \uc2 Usually, vertical rallies are followed by waterfall declines. The first support in an uptrend is the 20-day exponential moving average ($16,019), but if this support cracks, the correction could reach $14,000.\par \par \uc2 The relative strength index (RSI) has risen deep into overbought territory, suggesting a pullback may occur anytime.\par \par \uc2 However, when the momentum is strong, the price can stay overbought for an extended period; hence, investors should not try to call a top but protect their position with a suitable trailing stop-loss according to their trading strategy.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 As Bitcoin rallied to a multiyear high, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) broke out of the $488.134 resistance and cleared the psychological level at $500 for the first time since July 2018. This shows aggressive buying at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d9bcf653-4b55-4812-b51a-b97443662dab.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI close to the overbought territory suggest that bulls are in control. If the bulls can flip $488.134 to support during the next pullback, the ETH/USD pair may start its journey to $550 and then to $625.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears can pull the price below $488.134 during the next correction, it will indicate profit-booking at higher levels. A break below the 20-day EMA ($451) may suggest that the short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has ended.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The long tails on the Nov. 18 and 19 candlesticks suggest that bulls are buying on dips. So far, they have managed to push {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above the $0.303746 resistance, and next, they will try to drive the price above the overhead resistance at $0.326113.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d94003fc-bd24-4c59-b4f9-5178364aa1f9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the XRP/USD pair could rally to $0.40. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the overbought zone suggest that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears defend the overhead resistance, the pair may consolidate between $0.303746 and $0.326113 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 A break below the $0.303746 support could suggest a lack of buyers at higher levels. The bears will then try to sink the pair below the 20-day EMA ($0.272) and gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink's LINK broke out and closed above the $13.28 resistance on Nov. 18, which completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  inverse head-and-shoulders setup. This new uptrend has a pattern target of $19.2731.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/69d4af9b-50c0-46ad-ac26-d9cf13495faa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bears will try to stall the up-move close to $16 and pull the price back below the breakout level of $13.28. If they can sink the price below $11.80, it will suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap.\par \par \uc2 In an uptrend, the sentiment is to buy the dips. The rising moving averages and the RSI above 66 suggest that the bulls are in command. Hence, they are likely to buy the dip to the breakout level of $13.28 and flip it to support. If that happens, the uptrend could resume.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) has hit a new 52-week high today, above the overhead resistance at $84.3374. The strong rebound off the $68.9008 support on Nov. 18 shows that the bulls aggressively purchased the dip to the breakout level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/dbdc3ea2-15fb-407b-8261-24a23d96fedf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI has risen into the overbought zone, indicating that the bulls are in control. If the price sustains above $85, the rally may extend to $100. This level may act as a hurdle, but if crossed, the rally could reach $140.\par \par \uc2 However, during the previous two instances, a reading of close to 80 on the RSI resulted in a correction. Hence, traders should look out for the possibility of a minor correction in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 The trend in the LTC/USD pair could turn negative if the bears pull the price back below the breakout level of $68.9008.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) has held the $242 support for the past two days, which shows that bulls are buying at lower levels. If the buyers can push the price above $260, the altcoin may start its journey to the $272 and $280 resistance zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/91f5b5cc-5a66-4838-8a8d-fda3bb294f08.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The overhead zone may act as a stiff hurdle, but if the bulls can push the price above it, the BCH/USD pair could rally to $326.30, then to $337.90.\par \par \uc2 However, the flat 20-day EMA ($254) and the RSI near the midpoint suggest that the range-bound action between $242 and $272 may continue for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The advantage will shift in favor of the bears if the pair turns down from the current levels and slips below the $231 support.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot's DOT took support at the 20-day EMA ($4.54) over the past two days and has broken above the overhead resistance at $4.95 today. The upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the overbought zone suggest that bulls are in command.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/b81ceaa7-f7dd-45e8-bfb1-4a40e853127e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the buyers can propel the price above $5.5899, the DOT/USD pair may rally to $6.25, then to the highs at $6.8619.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to throw in the towel easily. They will try to stall the current rally at $5.5899. If they manage to do that, the pair could consolidate between $4.95 and $5.5899 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears drag the price back below the breakout level of $4.95 and the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has broken out of the $27.30\u8211\'20\'13$28.97 range it had been stuck in for the past few days, but the bulls are struggling to sustain the higher levels. This suggests that bears are attempting to keep the price inside the range.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/b7097654-cb8e-4095-a006-9a2c1de9453d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can sustain the breakout, a new up-move to the $32\u8211\'20\'13$33.3888 zone is possible. If the price turns down from this zone, the BNB/USD pair may extend its stay inside a large range.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the bulls can thrust the price above the resistance zone, the pair could retest the all-time highs at $39.5941.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the bulls fail to sustain the current breakout. In that case, the bears will try to pull the price below the $27.30 support, and if they succeed, the pair could drop to $25.6652.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls did not allow Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slip below the moving averages and the downtrend line in the past two days. This is a positive sign as it shows buying at lower levels. The altcoin has resumed its journey to the top of the range at $0.114241.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f5d8e2a5-3e4f-4dfb-8f6e-50a84b00586c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can drive the price above $0.1142241, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair could start a new uptrend that can rally to $0.1280, then to $0.1445.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone suggest that bulls have the upper hand. Traders can watch the RSI because a break above 60 could suggest that the rally may pick up momentum.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair once again turns down from the overhead resistance, the range-bound action could continue for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears could not sustain Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) below the downtrend line over the past two days. This shows that the bulls are accumulating at lower levels, and they have pushed the price back above the moving averages today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/61b5f2ed-c156-4bcb-a2ea-076199f981e5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The BSV/USD pair could now move up to $181. If the bears defend this resistance aggressively, the pair may extend its stay inside the range for a few more days. The flat moving averages and the RSI close to 54 suggest a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can drive the price above $181, the pair could start a new uptrend that has a target objective of $216. This positive view will be invalidated if the price turns down and plummets below the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvZTg0NTMyNjgtYTBkZS00NTljLThkYTktNDFkNmUwZTQ1MDI0LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201120egbk000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/18: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, LTC, BCH, DOT, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,924 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price looks ready to consolidate after reaching a new 2020 high and altcoins may attempt to recover from their sharp losses.\par \par \uc2 Within the last 24-hours, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price hit an intraday high of $18,466.14 and this is just roughly 8% lower than the magical $20,000 figure being watched by many traders.\par \par \uc2 However, investors in several countries such as Russia, Argentina, Brazil, and Mexico have already seen their Bitcoin holdings hit a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-has-hit-all-time-highs-against-numerous-world-currencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new all-time high}}}\uc2  in their local currency. Even Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-bitcoin-s-market-cap-just-hit-a-new-record-high-before-the-price-did"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 market capitalization}}}\uc2  has hit a new record high, topping the high created in December 2017.\par \par \uc2 With institutional investors finally arriving in herds, it seems it is only a matter of time before Bitcoin finally overtakes $20,000 and sets a new all-time high.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the list of high profile billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s acquiring Bitcoin, Ricardo Salinas Pliego, Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s second-richest man, recently announced that he had invested in the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Accordion to Pliego, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/mexico-s-second-richest-man-invests-10-of-his-liquid-portfolio-in-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10% of his liquid}}}\uc2  assets are held in Bitcoin.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/8d0ebb24-bee0-4bc7-8f0b-80dbbaeb69d5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Even existing investors have added to their holdings. Galaxy Digital chairman and CEO Mike Novogratz recently said that he had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-will-hit-65k-mike-novogratz-tells-actress-maisie-williams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 purchased more}}}\uc2  Bitcoin at $15,800 as he expects a rally to $65,000. Novogratz believes that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe network effect has taken over\u8221\'20\'1D and with \u8220\'20\'1Ctons of new buyers\u8221\'20\'1D coming in, the limited supply will not be enough.\par \par \uc2 The steady institutional inflow has resulted in Grayscale Investments Bitcoin holdings surging to over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-now-has-half-a-million-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 500,000 Bitcoin}}}\uc2 . An annual survey from the company revealed that about 38% of the respondents have bought Bitcoin in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-survey-connects-covid-19-pandemic-to-new-bitcoin-purchases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 past four months}}}\uc2 . 63% of these investors said that the coronavirus pandemic was the main factor that influenced their decision to purchase Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 After today\u8217\'20\'19s spectacular rally, many investors are searching for hints on whether Bitcoin will continue its uptrend or correct sharply from the current levels.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top-10 cryptocurrencies to see what the charts project.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) momentum was very strong in the past two days and while many investors believed that $17,200 would serve as a major resistance, the price sliced right through it with ease.\par \par \uc2 However, the cryptocurrency has been running hard since early October and it may soon tire out if it keeps proceeding at the current pace.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/cb1366b0-71f3-45b5-93ba-403daaf3523c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If it takes a break to regroup and then resume the uptrend, this would be a positive as it would all the current rally to have longer staying power. The price has currently formed a Doji candlestick and this shows there is indecision among the bulls and the bears.\par \par \uc2 If the price corrects to the 20-day exponential moving average ($15,528), placed just above the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level, it may be considered a healthy sign.\par \par \uc2 Even if the price does not correct, a range-bound action between $16,500 and $18,500 will be positive.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the momentum drives the BTC/USD pair to new highs without any pullback, then the possibility of the record highs sustaining will be lowered. At that time, a correction could be vicious as there is no major support until $12,500.\par \par \uc2 The relative strength index (RSI) has been trading between 70 and 84 for about a month, which shows that the trend is strong but also overextended. Hence, at the risk of missing out on some part of the rally, traders should keep their greed in check and trade with suitable stop losses.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) inched above the overhead resistance at $488.134 today but the bulls could not sustain the breakout. This shows that the bears are defending the overhead resistance aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/e67a8d7d-3f52-42e2-845d-eb77a5a6e33f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls do not allow the price to dip below the 20-day EMA ($442), it will suggest accumulation at lower levels. If the price consolidates near the overhead resistance, it will increase the possibility of a break above it.\par \par \uc2 If the ETH/USD pair sustains above $488.134, the rally could extend to $520 and then to $550.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the momentum has weakened. A break below the 50-day simple moving average ($399) will tilt the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  reached its first target objective at $0.303746 on Nov. 17 and short-term traders seem to have booked profits at this level as seen from the sharp correction today. However, the bulls are trying to arrest the decline at the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.278123.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/99ad1b12-323c-436a-8788-aaa2ceffeec2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, then another attempt to push the price above the $0.308176 resistance is likely. The next level where the bears may again launch a stiff resistance is $0.326113.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI near overbought territory suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the XRP/USD pair dips below $0.278123, a decline to the 20-day EMA ($0.264) is likely.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) broke above the $13.28 overhead resistance on Nov. 17 but the bulls are struggling to sustain the breakout. This suggests that the bears are attempting to sink the price back below the breakout level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/cbb70269-e1b9-46a7-9f66-82e3a72ac7d5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the LINK/USD pair breaks and sustains below the 20-day EMA ($12.26), it will invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  inverse head and shoulders pattern.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls manage to sustain the price above the breakout level of $13.28, the pair could start its journey towards the target objective of $19.2731. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 59 suggest that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) is currently witnessing a pullback in an uptrend but the long tail on the candlestick shows strong buying at the breakout level of $68.9008. This suggests that the bulls have managed to flip $68.9008 as support. This level may now act as a floor during future declines.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/17e3d5f6-c6eb-43c4-b53d-43c49644ce8e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone suggest that the bulls are in control. They will now attempt to push the price above the $77.20 resistance and resume the uptrend. If they succeed, the LTC/USD pair could rally to $100.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the bears sink the price below the immediate support at $68.9008, it will suggest that the momentum has weakened. A break below the 20-day EMA ($62.92) could signal that the bears have made a strong comeback.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) continues to face stiff resistance at the 20-day EMA ($255). This is a negative sign as it suggests that the bulls are not able to absorb the selling by the bears and push the price higher.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/37bb181b-5ce1-47e9-89a9-45a02ca1e462.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The price has broken below the moving averages and the bears will now try to sink the BCH/USD pair below the immediate support at $242. If they succeed, the pair could drop to the $231 support.\par \par \uc2 A break below $231 will increase the likelihood of a fall to $200 but if the pair rebounds off $231, the range-bound action may continue for a few more days. The flat moving averages and the RSI in the negative territory suggest a minor advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 20-day EMA ($4.41) on Nov. 16 and reached the overhead resistance at $4.95 on Nov. 17. The bears are currently trying to defend the resistance and keep the altcoin range-bound for a few more days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d4e31c8f-7b98-4e70-8903-2f1bf4c09278.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the gradually upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in positive territory suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the buyers may once again attempt to clear the hurdle at $4.95. If they can do that, the DOT/USD pair could move up to $5.5899.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair breaks below the moving averages, the range-bound action between $3.80 and $4.95 could continue for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls failed to propel Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) above the $27.30 to $28.97 range today as the price turned down from the overhead resistance. This suggests that buying dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/582173cb-40a0-4841-8797-fd5f36bbfa2a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, this tight range trading is unlikely to continue for long. Soon, the BNB/USD pair will either break above or below the range. It is difficult to predict the direction of the breakout because the indicators are suggesting a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, it is better to wait for the price to escape the range before placing large bets. If the bulls push the price above the range, a rally to $32 is possible. Conversely, if the bears sink the price below $27.30, the pair could retest the critical support at $25.6652.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above the downtrend line on Nov. 17 but they have not been able to clear the hurdle at $0.1142241. This suggests that the bears are defending this overhead resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/23105dfc-4ea3-4a9f-9b5d-bf9a3b8b073b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair does not dip back below the downtrend line, the bulls will once again try to propel the price above the overhead resistance. If they manage to do that, the pair will complete a double bottom pattern that has a target objective of $0.1391.\par \par \uc2 If the RSI breaks and sustains above 60, it could signal a possible pick up in momentum that could result in a break above $0.1142241. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair breaks below the $0.098822 support.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) rallied above the downtrend line on Nov. 17 but the bulls have not been able to sustain the momentum. This suggests that traders are closing their positions even on minor rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/3956d3e7-956e-4f20-88a0-703e3aca883f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears are currently trying to sink the BSV/USD pair back below the downtrend line, while the bulls are attempting to achieve a close above it. The flat moving averages and the RSI close to the midpoint does not give a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears.\par \par \uc2 A close above the downtrend line could increase the possibility of a rally to $181 while a close below the line may result in a drop to $146. The next trending move could start after the pair breaks above or below the $181 to $146 range.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvMzA3M2QxYWMtYzMxMi00YWZhLThhMjItOTc5YzNiODdkMDIwLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201118egbi000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/16: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, BCH, LTC, BNB, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,795 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has resumed its journey toward a new all-time high and the renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum is pulling altcoin prices higher.\par \par \uc2 As Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) continues to rally to a new 2020 high above $16,700, traders are pondering whether this is the start of a new bull market.\par \par \uc2 Mike McGlone, senior commodities strategist at Bloomberg Intelligence, believes that the main hurdle is at the all-time high near $20,000. Once that is crossed, Bitcoin could reach a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/1t-market-cap-is-next-big-resistance-for-bitcoin-bloomberg-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/1t-market-cap-is-next-big-resistance-for-bitcoin-bloomberg-analyst}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/1t-market-cap-is-next-big-resistance-for-bitcoin-bloomberg-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1 trillion market capitalization}}}\uc2 . McGlone anticipates the uptrend to continue in 2021, and there are a growing number of analysts who agree with his view.\par \par \uc2 Veteran trader Peter Brandt also believes that if previous bull runs are considered, Bitcoin is in the early stages of its next bull cycle.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d9780d2f-f0cd-401d-b1bb-43389488e03f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 In another \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  projection, Citibank managing director Tom Fitzpatrick believes that Bitcoin could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/citibank-makes-tentative-318k-bitcoin-prediction-for-december-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally to $318,000 by December 2021}}}\uc2 . Fitzpatrick arrived at this forecast by considering the previous bull markets in Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Every bull phase witnesses considerable corrections on the way up, and these provide opportunities for traders to sell high and buy again during dips. However, in order to do this, traders have to time their trades, otherwise they may miss out on the move.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top 10 cryptocurrencies to spot any \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  or \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setups that could project the next possible move.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 In a strong uptrend, corrections usually do not last more than three days. This can be seen in Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s rally that started in early October. The bulls have pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $16,500 and resumed the upward move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/bfcb1b3c-a6d9-4c7e-9d5a-de77a8059911.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The BTC/USD pair could now rally to the next significant resistance at $17,200. Here again, the bulls may have to overcome strong selling by the bears because once the buyers clear this resistance, there is no major hurdle until the all-time highs.\par \par \uc2 The rising moving averages and the relative strength index in overbought territory suggest that bulls are in control. There is no negative formation on the chart that warns of a possible top at the current juncture.\par \par \uc2 Still, traders should be careful and not get carried away with strength. They can keep a close eye on the 20-day exponential moving average ($15,032) because a break below it will be the first sign of weakness.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has been facing selling pressure at the resistance line of the rising wedge pattern. This line has now reached close to the overhead resistance at $488.134. Hence, the bears are likely to mount a strong defense of this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/3e4aefa6-ed34-495f-b4a1-e6730dbe0c92.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the overhead resistance and the bulls do not give up much ground, then it will increase the possibility of a breakout of $488.134. Above this level, the ETH/USD pair could rally to $520 and then to $550.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 61 suggest that bulls have the upper hand. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be negated if the price turns down from the current levels or the overhead resistance and plummets below the 20-day EMA ($435).\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  broke and closed above the $0.26 resistance on Nov. 13. Although the bears sold the rallies on Nov. 14 and 15, they could not pull the price back below the breakout level of $0.26.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/528d1101-b99a-4d10-ae06-d2460a4a4bcc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This shows that the sentiment has turned positive and the bulls are accumulating on dips. The 20-day EMA ($0.256) has turned up, and the RSI has reached the overbought zone, which suggests that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 The first target on the upside is $0.303746 and if this level is scaled, the XRP/USD pair could retest the $0.326113 resistance. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down and plummets below the $0.26 support.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink's LINK is currently attempting to bounce off the 20-day EMA ($12). The bulls will now again try to propel the price above the $13.28 overhead resistance. If they succeed, the altcoin will complete an inverse head-and-shoulders pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/1dcfb167-086d-4314-9043-432fad1ce20a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The target objective of this \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup is $19.2731. The gradually rising moving averages and the RSI just above the midpoint suggest a minor advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current levels or the overhead resistance and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the LINK/USD pair could drop to the 50-day simple moving average ($11). A break below $9.7665 will invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) once again turned down from the overhead resistance zone of $272 to $280 on Nov. 15. This shows that the bears are defending this level aggressively. If the bears can sink the price below the immediate support at $242, a drop to $231 is possible.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/47778c47-311c-433e-b568-4ced32d11c9b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($256) is flat, while the 50-day SMA ($249) is moving up, and the RSI has been trading between 40 and 60 levels. This suggests a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 Trading inside a range can be volatile and difficult to predict. Hence, it is better to trade when the price reaches the support or resistance of the range. Another possibility is to wait for the price to break above or below the range before taking large bets.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $280, the BCH/USD pair could rally to $326.30. Conversely, a drop below $231 may sink the price to $200.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) has soared and broken out of the overhead resistance at $68.9008. If the bulls can sustain the price above the breakout level, it will signal the possible start of a new uptrend. The next target on the upside is $80, then $100.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/55ae328c-e1be-4807-8f9d-e5f74c973142.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to give up easily. They will try to fake the current breakout and pull the price back below $68.9008. If they succeed, it will suggest strong selling close to the $70 mark.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below $68.9008, the bears will then try to drag the LTC/USD pair down to the $64 support. If they can do that, it will suggest that the upward momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to sink Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) below the tight range of $27.30 to $28.97. The downsloping 20-day EMA ($28.29) and the RSI below 47 suggest an advantage to the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/3b7c96e8-f0b5-4d58-967a-e2166ef2a6a5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the BNB/USD pair dips below $27.30, the next stop could be $25.6652. This is an important support, as the bulls have defended it aggressively on two previous occasions.\par \par \uc2 A strong rebound of this support will increase the possibility that the pair may consolidate in the $25.6652\u8211\'20\'13$32 range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair rebounds off the current levels and rises above the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again try to push the price above $28.97. If they succeed, a rally to $30 and then to $32 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot's DOT bounced off the 20-day EMA ($4.36) on Nov. 12, but the bulls could not push the price above the minor resistance at $4.63. This suggests a lack of demand at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/65852251-92d2-4902-b48f-88ce231bedbf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls have again purchased the dip to the 20-day EMA and are currently attempting to push the price above the immediate resistance at $4.63. If they manage to do that, the DOT/USD pair could rally to $4.95.\par \par \uc2 The marginally upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive territory suggest an advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the moving averages. In such a case, a drop to $3.80 is possible.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped below the moving averages on Nov. 15, but the bulls are trying to defend the support at $0.098822. If the altcoin rebounds and rises above the moving averages, the bulls will again try to push the price to $0.1142241.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/c2eee893-528b-4f8f-ace0-589254f61618.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close above the downtrend line will be the first sign of strength. Contrary to this assumption, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair turns down from the downtrend line and plummets below $0.098822, it could drop to $0.0893.\par \par \uc2 As the bulls had purchased the previous two declines to $0.0893, they are likely to attempt it again. Hence, a bounce off this support could extend the stay of the pair inside the range.\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI near the halfway mark also point to a range-bound action for the next few days.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV (BSV) again turned down from the 20-day EMA ($161) on Nov. 14, which suggests that the bears are selling on minor rallies. If the selling continues, the altcoin could drop to the critical support at $146.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d2c74536-e28b-447f-86c1-ed77ce9356db.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI below 49 suggest a minor advantage to the bears. However, one positive development is the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence on the RSI. This suggests that the downside momentum may be weakening.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above the downtrend line, it could clear the path for a rally to $181. The next trending move is likely to start after the bulls drive the price above $181 or the bears sink the price below $146.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvOGQxYzI0ZDQtMjkwMS00YTQ4LWFlZDMtMDViMDg1OWJiODcxLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201116egbg000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/13: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, BCH, LTC, BNB, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,795 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A few altcoins are trying to start a new up-move even though Bitcoin is struggling to pull above $16,300.\par \par \uc2 Data shows that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) current rally is supported by greater participation from retail and institutional investors. The CME Bitcoin futures open interest has moved closer to the previous all-time high, a sign that institutional investors are becoming more interested in cryptocurrencies. Similarly, Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s spot {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-surge-to-16-2k-accompanied-by-record-volume-data-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 volume has hit a new 52-week high, according to data from Arcane research}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, during strong uptrends, traders tend to get greedy and take on excessive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-futures-and-options-suggest-that-a-major-btc-price-move-is-looming"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leverage}}}\uc2 . Hence, large open interest on derivatives could act as a double-edged sword because even a small decline in Bitcoin could force the highly leveraged traders to close their positions. Such a move could have a cascading effect that could lead to long liquidation.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6d80f844-29e5-4a9f-b63b-b8c08ff7c985.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 While traders should be cautious, there is no need to panic as yet because the current up-move in Bitcoin has happened without any euphoria or frenzy, especially among retail traders.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, several analysts have been skeptical of the rally, which is another positive sign. The top usually forms when the last bear in the market turns \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  and there is no one left to buy.\par \par \uc2 This does not mean that there will be no corrections along the way. Pullbacks are necessary to periodically shake out the weak hands and this generally improves the longevity of the trend.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the top-10 cryptocurrencies to ascertain whether the uptrend will continue or is a correction around the corner.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) above the $16,000 overhead resistance on Nov. 12. This breakout started the next leg of the uptrend that may carry the price to the critical overhead resistance at $17,200.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/a4a40375-5fce-4519-b785-b8c896956c31.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the relative strength index in the overbought territory suggest that the bulls are in command. If the momentum can carry the price above $17,200, then the bulls will have a clear shot at the all-time highs.\par \par \uc2 However, traders can get cautious if the pair turns down from the current levels and drops below $16,000 once again. This will suggest that the market participants have rejected higher levels.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below $16,000, the bears will try to sink the BTC/USD pair below the 20-day exponential moving average ($14,596). Such a move will indicate that bulls are not buying the dips as the sentiment has turned negative.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are finding it difficult to propel Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) above the resistance line of the rising wedge pattern. However, the positive thing is that the bulls have not given up much ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/01f56722-a21a-4784-a730-017075dabbe7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls will again attempt to thrust the price above the wedge. If they can do that, the ETH/USD pair may rise to $488.134. The bears may again try to stall the up-move at this resistance. If they succeed, a drop to the 20-day EMA ($426) is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls can push the price above $488.134, the next leg of the uptrend is likely to begin. The first target on the upside is $520 and then $550. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 67 suggest that bears are in command.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break below the 20-day EMA. Such a move could result in a drop to the support line of the wedge.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  has been consolidating near the $0.26 overhead resistance for the past two days. This suggests that the bulls are not closing their positions in a hurry as they expect the price to break above the range.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/61554e7f-a2aa-4e3f-82fb-9de05468366a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising moving averages and the RSI above 59 suggest that bulls are in control. A breakout and close above $0.26 could start the journey to $0.30. Above this level, the up-move may reach $0.326113.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bulls again fail to sustain the price above $0.26, then the bears will try to pull the price back below the moving averages. If they succeed, the XRP/USD pair may drop to $0.2295.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls failed to push and sustain Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) above $13.28 on Nov. 11. This shows that the bears are aggressively defending this resistance. However, the positive thing is that the bulls have not given up much ground in the past two days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/b5f767bb-4f2e-4d57-87e2-254e1797f4ea.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to drive the price above $13.28. If they manage to do that, the LINK/USD pair will complete an inverse head and shoulders pattern that has a target objective of $19.2731.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI has risen above 58. This suggests a minor advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair turns down from $13.28 once again, the bears will try to pull the price down to $9.7665. A break below this support will invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip below the 20-day EMA ($257) on Nov. 12 but could not sustain the higher levels. This has attracted selling by the bears and Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) has broken below the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/53c3550f-5f3b-4bca-91d1-96d9393ae55c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 50-day simple moving average ($247), the BCH/USD pair could drop to the next support at $231. The bulls have defended this support on two previous occasions, hence, a break below it may intensify selling and drag the price to $200.\par \par \uc2 However, the 20-day EMA is flat and the RSI is close to the midpoint, which suggests a few more days of range-bound action. The momentum could pick up if the bulls push the price above $280 or the bears sink the price below $231.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) has surged above the $64 resistance today, which shows that the bulls have overpowered the bears. The buyers will now try to sustain the momentum and drive the price above $68.9008.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6bfc6dc3-44b1-4d47-a9cd-2a6b15b50674.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the next leg of the uptrend could begin. The next target is $80 and then a rally to $100 is possible. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 67 suggest bulls are in charge.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price again turns down from the current levels and plummets below $64, it will suggest a lack of buyers at higher levels. Such a move could attract profit booking that may result in a drop to the 20-day EMA ($57.86).\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) is currently stuck in a tight range between $28.97 and $27.30. The altcoin bounced off the support of this range on Nov. 12 and the bulls will now try to push the price above the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d29324db-c091-4763-b7f2-176b5ba08bee.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the BNB/USD pair could rise to $30 and a break above this resistance may open the gates for a rally to $32.\par \par \uc2 However, the downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI just below the midpoint suggest a minor advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current levels and breaks below $27.30, the pair may drop to $25.6652. A break below this support will signal weakness.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) turned down from $4.63 on Nov. 11 and the bears attempted to sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($4.31) on Nov. 12 but failed. This shows that bulls are defending the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d0da5f38-56f4-45cf-b35d-bff312f2de7d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is rising gradually and the RSI is above 55, which suggests that bulls have the upper hand. However, the buyers will have to sustain the price above the immediate resistance at $4.50 to increase the possibility of a move to $4.95.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the DOT/USD pair again turns down from $4.50 or $4.63, the bears will try to sink the price below the moving averages. If they succeed, the pair could drop to the $3.80 support.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 After the bulls failed to push Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) higher on Nov. 10 and 11, the bears tried to sink the price below the moving averages on Nov. 12 but could not. The altcoin has currently rebounded off the 20-day EMA ($0.102) and the bulls are attempting to push the price to $0.1142241.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/e4154298-7711-4c1d-bff2-0b19267ba573.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are rising and the RSI is in the positive zone, suggesting an advantage to the bulls. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair could pick up momentum after the bulls push the price above $0.1142241.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair turns down from the current levels and plunges below the moving averages, the bears will try to pull the price down to the $0.0893 support.\par \par \uc2 The next trending move may start after the bulls push the price above $0.1142241 or the bears sink the price below $0.0893.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls have failed to propel Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($162) in the past three days. This suggests a lack of urgency among the bulls to buy at the current levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/1f4b2fbe-1169-474b-8cfa-a24f0fcda8de.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI is just below the midpoint, which suggests a minor advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 If the sellers can sink the price below the immediate support at $154.66, the BSV/USD pair could drop to the $146 support.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the bulls can push the price above the moving averages and the downtrend line. Such a move will increase the possibility of a rally to $181.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvN2VhMjZmNGMtN2ZkZC00ZDQ3LTljNjEtZTg4MGRjNmU1ZjRiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201113egbd000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Impending CME gap close could propel Bitcoin price to $18,000\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ray Salmond \par \uc2 654 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin bulls are aiming to close the overhead CME gap in order to create a path to $18,000.\par \par \uc2 Within the last hour, the Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price surged through the $16,200 level to secure a new 2020 high at $16,473.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/51929905-6093-4f39-af22-7105ff7976d2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 6.62% move brings the top-ranked \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  closer to closing a CME gap in the $16,465 to $16,570 zone and a growing number of analysts expect the price to break above the $17,200 level if the CME gap is closed.\par \par \uc2 Despite the excitement surrounding Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s surge to a new multi-year high, Cointelegraph contributor Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe pointed out that Bitcoin has rapidly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/can-bitcoin-price-conquer-16-000-as-extreme-greed-grips-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ascended to new highs without establishing strong supports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Van de Poppe said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany levels beneath the current price are untested on the weekly timeframe. A healthy way to build up a new cycle is the backtesting of previous resistance levels as new areas of support.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The analyst also said that the Crypto Fear and Greed Index has reached the \u8220\'20\'1CExtreme Greed\u8221\'20\'1D level, which can be interpreted as a sell signal.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/27c2b47f-f89b-4d17-88fd-ce5d6549c03b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto Fear and Greed Index. Source: Digital Assets Data\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s impressive rally to $16,465 comes as the Dow and S&P 500 closed the day in the red with a 1.08% and 0.97% loss.\par \par \uc2 While stocks had initially surged after President Elect Joe Biden was declared the winner of the U.S. election, coronavirus infections across the country have risen to a record 150,000 infections per day over the past few days, which in turn has made investors fearful that a new phase of economic shutdowns could be announced.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also possible that President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to concede the election and the prospect of divided government under a Biden administration could be negatively weighing on investors\u8217\'20\'19 confidence in the future of traditional markets.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has largely ignored the downturn in stocks and the increasing spread of COVID-19, with the token\u8217\'20\'19s price up 26.78% in November and 127.7% year-to-date.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/cd9107de-fc51-4ebf-9b5a-0e80e29c79a5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Macro assets\u8217\'20\'19 current year returns. Source: Skew\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  news like \uc2 PayPal\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that it had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/paypal-s-crypto-goes-live-in-the-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nixed its waiting list}}}\uc2  for clients looking to trade cryptocurrencies is surely working in Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s favor.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 PayPal\uc2 , crypto payments will soon be available to 26 million merchants globally, and the payments giant also raised the trading cap for U.S.-based customers from $10,000 to $20,000 per week.\par \par \uc2 Given \uc2 PayPal\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s immense user base, analysts are watching for an influx of new Bitcoin investors, as the implementation will likely result in increased demand and push the price even higher.\par \par \uc2 DeFi 2.0?\par \par \uc2 In other news, the DeFi revival continued as Uniswap again saw a strong surge in liquidity, bringing the figure to a record $3.2 billion.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/0781911c-2dd3-463b-baa7-686ef9abf27d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Uniswap liquidity (USD). Source: Uniswap\par \par \uc2 Data from DeFi Pulse also shows that the total value locked in DeFi platforms has soared to $13.65 billion. This is another sign that investors are reigniting their interest in DeFi tokens, farming projects and many of the other opportunities that exist in the sector.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/5680d624-c2ac-4c40-96bc-0a2b1f837ef8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total value locked in DeFi (USD). Source: DeFi Pulse\par \par \uc2 While Bitcoin price and volumes on an assortment of DeFi platforms have been on the rise, altcoins have seen marginal gains. Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) moved up 1.29% to trade above $460 again, and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) added 7.97%. Chainlink (LINK) was one of the stronger performers, rallying 12% to trade at $12.65.\par \par \uc2 According to CoinMarketCap, the overall cryptocurrency market cap now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stands}}}\uc2  at $466.5 billion, with Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s dominance rate at 65.4%.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvOTUzODQ3YzctYjFiZC00NmZiLTg0ZTQtZTlhZTE2MzU5NTkxLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201113egbd0005v\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Impending CME gap close could propel Bitcoin price to $18,000\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ray Salmond \par \uc2 666 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin bulls are aiming to close the overhead CME gap in order to create a path to $18,000.\par \par \uc2 Within the last hour Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price surged through the $16,200 level to secure a new 2020 high at $16,473.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/51929905-6093-4f39-af22-7105ff7976d2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 6.62% move brings the top-ranked \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  closer to closing a CME gap in the $16,465 to $16,570 zone and a growing number of analysts expect the price to break above the $17,200 level if the CME gap is closed.\par \par \uc2 Despite the excitement surrounding Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s surge to a new multi-year high, Cointelegraph contributor Micheal van de Poppe pointed out that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/can-bitcoin-price-conquer-16-000-as-extreme-greed-grips-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin has rapidly ascended to new highs without establishing strong supports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Van de Poppe said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany levels beneath the current price are untested on the weekly timeframe. A healthy way to build up a new cycle is the backtesting of previous resistance levels as new areas of support.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The analyst also said that the Crypto Fear and Greed Index has reached the \u8220\'20\'1CExtreme Greed\u8221\'20\'1D level, which can be interpreted as a sell signal according to Van de Poppe.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/27c2b47f-f89b-4d17-88fd-ce5d6549c03b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto Fear and Greed Index. Source: Digital Assets Data\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s impressive rally to $16,465 comes as the Dow and S&P 500 closed the day in the red with a 1.08% and 0.97% loss.\par \par \uc2 While stocks had initially surged after President Elect Joe Biden was declared the winner of the U.S. election but over the past few days coronavirus infections have risen to a record 150,000 infections per day which in turn has made investors fearful that a new phase of econoimc shutdowns could be announced.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also possible that President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to concede the election and the prospect of divided government under a Biden Administration could be negatively weighing on investors\u8217\'20\'19 confidence in the future of traditional markets.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has largely ignored the downturn in stocks and the increasing spread of COVID-19 and at the time of writing the cryptocurrency is up 26.78% in November and 127.7% year-to-date.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/cd9107de-fc51-4ebf-9b5a-0e80e29c79a5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Macro assets current year returns (%). Source: Skew\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  news like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/paypal-s-crypto-goes-live-in-the-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PayPal\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that it had nixed its waiting list}}}\uc2  for clients looking to trade cryptocurrencies is surely working in Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s favor.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 PayPal\uc2 , crypto payments will soon be available to 26 million merchants globally and the payments giant also raised the trading cap for U.S.-based customers from $10,000 to $20,000 per week.\par \par \uc2 Given that \uc2 PayPal\uc2  has an immense users base, analysts are watching to see if there is an influx of new Bitcoin investors as this will likely result in increased demand and push the price even higher.\par \par \uc2 DeFi 2.0?\par \par \uc2 In other news, the DeFi revival continued as Uniswap again saw a strong surge in liquidity, bringing the figure to a record $3.2 billion.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/0781911c-2dd3-463b-baa7-686ef9abf27d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Uniswap liquidity (USD). Source: Uniswap\par \par \uc2 Data from DeFi Pulse also shows that the total value locked in DeFi platforms has soared to a $13.65 billion. This is another sign that investors are reigniting their interest in DeFi tokens, farming projects and many of the other opportunities that exist in the sector.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/5680d624-c2ac-4c40-96bc-0a2b1f837ef8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total value locked in DeFi (USD). Source: DeFi Pulse\par \par \uc2 While Bitcoin price and volumes at an assortment of DeFi platforms have been on the rise, altcoins have seen marginal gains. Ether (ETH) moved up 1.29% to trade above $460 again, and Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) added 7.97%. Chainlink (LINK) was one of the stronger performers, rallying 12% to trade at $12.65.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinMarketCap}}}\uc2 , the overall cryptocurrency market cap now stands at $466.5 billion and Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s dominance rate is 65.4%.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvOTUzODQ3YzctYjFiZC00NmZiLTg0ZTQtZTlhZTE2MzU5NTkxLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201113egbd00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/11: BTC, ETH, XRP, LINK, BCH, BNB, DOT, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,781 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and several altcoins are showing signs of breaking above their overhead resistance levels, which suggests bulls remain in control.\par \par \uc2 Billionaire investor Stanley Druckenmiller became the latest famous name to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-may-pay-out-more-than-gold-says-billionaire-investor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disclose a Bitcoin position}}}\uc2 . Although Druckenmiller did not specify the quantity he had purchased, he did say that Bitcoin will outperform gold a lot more \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause it\u8217\'20\'19s thinner, more illiquid, and has a lot more beta to it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Paul Tudor Jones, Stanley Druckenmiller, and Bill Miller are some of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-billionaires-are-suddenly-accumulating-bitcoin-after-113-ytd-gain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most successful}}}\uc2  traders and investors on Wall Street. A stamp of approval from them is likely to attract several other investors who may want to diversify their portfolio and outperform the markets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/2f2731c9-c302-4c3c-9abc-e4f5288cf07b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 In further validation for the crypto space, controversial Australian politician Cory Bernardi has called Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) \u8220\'20\'1Cthe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/aussie-trump-invests-in-bitcoin-as-it-s-the-millennial-version-of-gold"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 millennial\u8217\'20\'19s version of gold}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D Even though Bernardi said that risks remain, he believes they are similar to that of any other asset class.\par \par \uc2 Alex Saunders, founder of the crypto education site \uc2 Nuggets\uc2  News, views the endorsements for cryptocurrencies by high-profile figures as a sign of changing times and earlier this week the analyst predicted that Bitcoin price will reach $1 million by 2030.\par \par \uc2 These fundamental points are long-term positives for cryptocurrency prices. However, let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out the path of least resistance in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) had formed an inside day candlestick pattern on Nov. 10, which showed indecision among the bulls and the bears. The uncertainty has been resolved to the upside today with the bulls attempting to push the price above the $16,000 resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6b4a6d4f-f40d-4eb8-a121-808b73fa7f7c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls succeed, the BTC/USD pair could start the journey towards the next target objective at $17,200. This level is likely to be the last stop before the pair retests the all-time highs.\par \par \uc2 The rising moving averages and the relative strength index in the overbought zone suggest that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price fails to sustain above $16,000, then the pair could remain range-bound between $14,000 and $16,000 for a few more days. A break below the 20-day exponential moving average ($14,242) will be the first sign of weakness.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) formed inside day candlestick patterns for three consecutive days from Nov. 8 to 10. This uncertainty has today resolved to the upside, which suggests that the bulls have absorbed the selling and have established their supremacy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/a88c4641-e793-4769-a941-a09c3a7772f9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can sustain the price above the resistance line of the wedge, it will invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. That will open the gates for a retest of the critical overhead resistance at $488.134. A breakout and close above this level could resume the up-move.\par \par \uc2 The first target on the upside is $520 and if the ETH/USD pair can ascend this level, a move to $550 is possible. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory suggest that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current levels and breaks below the 20-day EMA ($418), it will signal that the bears are aggressively defending the wedge. They will then try to pull the price down to the 50-day simple moving average at $382.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above the overhead resistance at $0.26 on Nov.10 but failed to sustain the breakout. This suggests selling at higher levels, but the positive thing is that the bulls have not allowed the price to break below the moving averages on the downside.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/9095fafc-94ce-41d4-8eb8-ffb34120d759.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Repeated jumps above a resistance level tend to weaken it. The bulls are currently again attempting to propel the XRP/USD pair above $0.26. If they succeed in sustaining the price above this level, a new uptrend is likely.\par \par \uc2 The first target on the upside is $0.30. The RSI in the positive territory and the gradually upsloping 20-day EMA ($0.248) suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the price turns down from the current levels and breaks below the moving averages. Such a move could drag the pair down to the support at $0.2295.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) has been trading close to the overhead resistance at $13.28 for the past few days. A tight consolidation near a resistance usually ends with a breakout favoring the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/5f0ee486-a9dd-4af6-b3e0-21fdfaba8474.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price closes above $13.28, it will complete an inverse head and shoulders pattern that may signal the start of a new up-move. The target objective of this setup is $19.2731.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory suggest that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price turns down sharply from the current levels. Such a move could result in profit-booking by short-term traders. A break below $9.7665 will signal a possible deeper correction to $7.30.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) is struggling to rebound off the 20-day EMA ($257). This suggests a lack of urgency among the bulls to buy at these levels as they may not be confident that the altcoin will rise above $280.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/2b77f747-cd96-40f4-97f8-cd0eea1166a0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence on the RSI also suggests that the momentum may be weakening. If the 20-day EMA support cracks, the BCH/USD pair could drop to the 50-day SMA ($245) and then to $231.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the pair rebounds off the current levels and breaks above the $272 to $280 resistance zone. The flattish 20-day EMA and the RSI close to the midpoint suggest a range-bound action in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The intraday range in Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) is narrowing, which suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears. The flat moving averages and the RSI just below the midpoint also suggests a balance between the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d18346bc-bbf5-4260-8b02-06b3cfbf5936.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the range expands to the upside and the bulls push the price above the moving averages and the overhead resistance at $30, the BNB/USD pair could rally to the $32 to $33.3888 zone.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the range expansion happens to the downside, the bears will try to sink the pair below the $25.6652 support.\par \par \uc2 The next trending move could start after the bulls push the price above $33.3888 or the bears sink the price below $25.6652.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) is currently stuck close to the midpoint of the $3.80 to $4.95 range. However, as long as the price sustains above the moving averages, the bulls will try to push the price to the resistance of the range.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/0ad4485d-43bc-43c4-b13c-60f0f5912d68.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The gradually upsloping 20-day EMA ($4.29) and the RSI in the positive zone suggest a marginal advantage to the bulls. A break above $4.95 could push the price to the next resistance at $5.5899.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price again turns down from $4.95, the DOT/USD pair may remain range-bound for a few more days. A break below the moving averages will be the first sign that the bulls have surrendered the advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) has bounced off the 20-day EMA ($56.75), which suggests that the sentiment remains positive and the bulls are buying on dips. The bulls will now try to push the price to the overhead resistance at $64.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/9cbfff0d-3d48-426f-bbff-2c689d9201f7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Traders can keep an eye on the RSI as it has formed a symmetrical triangle. A breakout of the triangle will increase the possibility of a break above $64 while a break below the triangle could pull the price below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone suggest that bulls have the upper hand. This advantage could shift in favor of the bears if the support at $56.50 gives way. Such a move could drag the LTC/USD pair to $51.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been sustaining above the moving averages for the past few days. The bulls are now likely to attempt to push the price above the overhead resistance at $0.1142241.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/fd8dd713-cb8e-4a78-a943-df7459b3de9e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair will complete a double bottom pattern that has a target objective of $0.1391. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory suggest an advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from $0.1142241, the pair may remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The advantage will tilt in favor of the bears if the price reverses direction and breaks below the moving averages. If that happens, the pair could drop to the critical support at $0.0893.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) remains range-bound but the failure of the bulls to push the price above the moving averages suggests a lack of demand at higher levels. The bears will now try to sink the price to the critical support at $146.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/b63396ac-d7cf-4134-984d-acfb994701f8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both the moving averages are flat and the RSI is just below the midpoint, which suggests a balance between supply and demand. Even if the BSV/USD pair dips to $146, the bulls are likely to defend this level.\par \par \uc2 A strong bounce off the support of the range could extend the stay inside the range. Contrary to this assumption, if the BSV/USD pair turns up from the current levels and breaks above the downtrend line, then it can move up to $181.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvZTU3MjczYjktZWM2MC00MjJmLTkyMDctOTQ5OTcwZWRlNmE2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201111egbb000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/9: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BNB, LTC, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,824 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price is recovering well from its 6% drop to $14,800 but top altcoins are slow to follow.\par \par \uc2 Professional traders are often perceived to be the smartest, as they weigh the risks before investing in an asset class. Opposite to that, most retail traders only keep an eye on the possible profits and disregard the risk before investing.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, the increase in the number of Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) addresses holding more than 100 Bitcoin to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/silicon-valley-and-smart-money-are-behind-this-bitcoin-rally-data-suggests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven-month high, at 16,271}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/silicon-valley-and-smart-money-are-behind-this-bitcoin-rally-data-suggests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/silicon-valley-and-smart-money-are-behind-this-bitcoin-rally-data-suggests}}}\uc2 , could be considered as a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sign. Furthermore, the low search volume for the keyword \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin\u8221\'20\'1D suggests that the current rally lacks the frenzied retail buying seen during the previous bull market in 2017.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/be0f4641-71ae-4385-9ae2-2d42a0f9e8df.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 PlanB, the creator of the stock-to-flow model, has maintained his \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance on Bitcoin, as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/s2f-creator-has-no-doubt-bitcoin-will-hit-100k-by-december-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expects the price to at least rally to $100,000}}}\uc2  by December 2021. If that happens, Bitcoin would command a market capitalization of about $2 trillion.\par \par \uc2 While crypto analysts are voicing \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts for Bitcoin, noted economist and Bitcoin skeptic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cbdc-revolution-is-coming-in-3-years-says-bitcoin-naysayer-roubini"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nouriel Roubini remains \b  \highlight22bearish\b0 \highlight22 }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cbdc-revolution-is-coming-in-3-years-says-bitcoin-naysayer-roubini"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/cbdc-revolution-is-coming-in-3-years-says-bitcoin-naysayer-roubini}}}\uc2 , as he anticipates central bank digital currencies to start a big revolution in about three years. Thereafter, \u8220\'20\'1CNot only you don\u8217\'20\'19t need crypto, you don\u8217\'20\'19t even need Venmo,\u8221\'20\'1D said Roubini in a recent interview.\par \par \uc2 In other news, U.S. equity markets surged higher on the positive news that \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-dumps-on-news-of-successful-covid-19-vaccine-trials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recording success in its COVID-19 vaccine trials}}}\uc2 . As the news broke, gold and Bitcoin prices corrected sharply, but it appears that crypto investors are viewing the dips as buying opportunities.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s take a look at the top crypto assets to see how they are performing today.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) is in an uptrend but is currently facing stiff resistance near $16,000. The failure to rise above the overhead resistance could attract profit-booking from the short-term traders and shorting by the aggressive bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f80b652b-c207-4bab-8574-a2e5c261b672.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the BTC/USD pair breaks below $15,650, it could drop to the critical support at $14,000. The 20-day exponential moving average ($13,935) is placed just below this support; hence, the bulls are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 A strong bounce off the 20-day EMA will indicate accumulation by the bulls at lower levels. The price could remain stuck between $14,000 and $16,000 for a few days before starting the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $16,000, a rally to $17,200 and then to all-time highs is possible. Conversely, a break below the 20-day EMA could result in a fall to the 50-day simple moving average ($12,137).\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to push the price above the resistance line of the rising wedge pattern. Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) formed an inside day candlestick pattern on Nov. 8 and is currently trading in a tight range. This suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/a0ea1707-0544-4d24-b65f-5a2a6285ad24.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $432, the possibility of a drop to the 20-day EMA ($409) increases. A break below the support line of the wedge will indicate an advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping 20-day EMA and the relative strength index in the positive zone suggest an advantage to the bulls. If they can push the price above the wedge, the ETH/USD pair could rally to $488.134.\par \par \uc2 A breakout of this resistance could resume the uptrend with the next target at $520 and then $550.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  attempted to break out of the range on Nov. 7 but the bears pushed the price right back in. The bulls are currently attempting to defend the moving averages. If they succeed, another attempt to push the price above $0.26 is likely.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7b50b13a-04c2-4d0d-a97d-e97f2ab8aebd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains above $0.26 for a day, the XRP/USD pair could start a new uptrend with the first target objective at $0.30.\par \par \uc2 However, the flat moving averages and the RSI near the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. If the price slips below the moving averages, the pair could remain range-bound between $0.26 and $0.2295 for the next few days.\par \par \uc2 A break below the $0.2295 to $0.219712 support zone will tilt the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) broke above $272 for the past two days but could not sustain the higher levels. The repeated price rejection shows that the bears are aggressively defending the $272\u8211\'20\'13$280 resistance zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/58976808-33d8-4947-b5fe-2dc16d471a77.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($257), the BCH/USD pair could drop to $242 and then to $231. Such a move will indicate the possibility of a range-bound action between $231 and $280 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone suggest a minor advantage to the bulls. If the bulls can push the price above the overhead resistance zone, a rally to $300 and then to $326.30 is possible.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls tried to propel Chainlink's LINK above the $13.28 resistance on Nov. 7 but failed. However, the positive thing is that the altcoin bounced off the 20-day EMA ($11.46) and the bulls are again trying to push the price above the overhead resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/0ebce3dc-3cd1-4bd4-b25b-a5df6aad8229.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  inverse head-and-shoulders pattern that has a target objective of $19.2731. The 20-day EMA ($11.46) has started to turn up gradually, and the RSI is in the positive territory, which suggests a minor advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 However, if the price again turns down from the overhead resistance, the bears will try to sink the LINK/USD pair below the moving averages. If they succeed, a drop to $9.7665 is possible.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has been stuck between $32 and $25.6652 for the past few days. The bulls attempted to push the price above the moving averages on Nov. 7, but they failed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f9098693-32a2-4a34-8057-8c64743cfb6f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($28) and the RSI in negative territory suggest that bears have the upper hand. If the price sustains below the moving averages, a drop to $25.6652 is possible.\par \par \uc2 A bounce off this support could extend the stay inside the range for a few more days, while a break below it could start a new downtrend.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the BNB/USD pair turns up from the current levels and breaks above $30. Such a move could result in a rally to $32.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) once again turned down from the stiff overhead resistance of $64 on Nov. 7. Barring the breakout on Aug. 17, the price has turned down from this resistance on three occasions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/158d0c60-4d8e-47f4-8de3-5af648bf2a35.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The RSI is forming a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence, which suggests that the momentum may be weakening.\par \par \uc2 If the LTC/USD pair turns down from the current levels or the overhead resistance and plummets below the 20-day EMA ($56), it will increase the possibility of a drop to the 50-day SMA ($50).\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above $64. If they succeed, a rally to $68.9008 is possible.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot's DOT is currently trading inside a small range that has resistance at $4.95 and support at $3.80. The price turned down from $4.8586 on Nov. 7, which shows that the bears are aggressively defending this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/4edf163b-9db0-4925-99b9-93d58bd1a24c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls are trying to keep the price above the moving averages, and the RSI has also taken support at the 50 level. If the RSI can break out of the downtrend line, it will indicate an advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If buyers can push the price above $4.95, a rally to $5.5899 is likely. The bears may again defend this level aggressively, but if the bulls can thrust the price above it, a new uptrend could begin.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  turned down from the $0.1142241 resistance on Nov. 7, which shows that the bears are aggressively defending this level. However, the positive thing is that the bulls have not allowed the price to dip below the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/def2c6ee-b630-4f33-bf59-7414d743cc18.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The strong rebound off the moving averages on Nov. 8 shows that the sentiment is to buy the dips. The bulls will again attempt to push the price above the overhead resistance. If they can pull it off, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair could rally to $0.128 and then to $0.1445.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price again turns down from $0.1142241, then the range-bound action may continue for a few more days. A break below the moving averages will signal weakness, and the bears will then try to sink the pair below $0.0893.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV (BSV) continues to trade inside the broad range of $146 to $181. The price has been oscillating above and below the moving averages for the past three days, which shows that traders are undecided about the next move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/43562f6f-bcfe-49d8-824c-bdcfac00ca82.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI close to the halfway mark suggest a balance between supply and demand. If the price sustains below the moving averages, the bears will try to sink the BSV/USD pair to the critical support at $146.\par \par \uc2 A rebound off this level could extend the range-bound action for a few more days. The trend will shift in favor of the bulls if they can push the price above the overhead resistance at $181.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by exchange {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvZDNlZTA5ZjktZTMyMi00YjUyLTgwNzItZTM4NTY2NGM5MWI3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201109egb9000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/9: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BNB, LTC, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,791 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price is recovering well from its 6% drop to $14,800 but top altcoins are slow to follow.\par \par \uc2 Professional traders are often perceived to be the smartest as they weigh the risks before investing in an asset class. Opposite to that, most retail traders only keep an eye on the possible profits and disregard the risk before investing.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, the increase in the number of Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) addresses holding more than 100 Bitcoin to a seven-month high, at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/silicon-valley-and-smart-money-are-behind-this-bitcoin-rally-data-suggests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16,271}}}\uc2 , could be considered as a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sign. Furthermore, the low search volume for the keyword \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin\u8221\'20\'1D suggests that the current rally lacks the frenzied retail buying seen during the previous bull market in 2017.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/be0f4641-71ae-4385-9ae2-2d42a0f9e8df.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 PlanB, the creator of the stock-to-flow model, has maintained his \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance on Bitcoin as he expects the price to at least rally to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/s2f-creator-has-no-doubt-bitcoin-will-hit-100k-by-december-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $100,000}}}\uc2  by December 2021. If that happens, Bitcoin would command a market capitalization of about $2 trillion.\par \par \uc2 While crypto analysts are voicing \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts for Bitcoin, noted economist and Bitcoin skeptic Nouriel Roubini remains {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cbdc-revolution-is-coming-in-3-years-says-bitcoin-naysayer-roubini"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22bearish\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  as he anticipates central bank digital currencies to start a big revolution in about three years. Thereafter, \u8220\'20\'1Cnot only you don\u8217\'20\'19t need crypto, you don\u8217\'20\'19t even need Venmo,\u8221\'20\'1D said Roubini in a recent interview.\par \par \uc2 In other news, U.S. equity markets surged higher on the positive news that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-dumps-on-news-of-successful-covid-19-vaccine-trials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pfizer is recording success in its COVID-19 vaccine trials}}}\uc2 . As the news broke, gold and Bitcoin prices corrected sharply but it appears that crypto investors are viewing the dips as buying opportunities.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s take a look at the top crypto assets to see how they are performing today.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) is in an uptrend but is currently facing stiff resistance near $16,000. The failure to rise above the overhead resistance could attract profit booking from the short-term traders and shorting by the aggressive bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f80b652b-c207-4bab-8574-a2e5c261b672.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the BTC/USD pair breaks below $15,650, it could drop to the critical support at $14,000. The 20-day exponential moving average ($13,935) is placed just below this support, hence, the bulls are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 A strong bounce off the 20-day EMA will indicate accumulation by the bulls at lower levels. The price could remain stuck between $14,000 and $16,000 for a few days before starting the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $16,000, a rally to $17,200 and then to the all-time highs is possible. Conversely, a break below the 20-day EMA could result in a fall to the 50-day simple moving average ($12,137).\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to push the price above the resistance line of the rising wedge pattern. Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) formed an inside day candlestick pattern on Nov. 8 and is currently trading in a tight range. This suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/a0ea1707-0544-4d24-b65f-5a2a6285ad24.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $432, the possibility of a drop to the 20-day EMA ($409) increases. A break below the support line of the wedge will indicate an advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping 20-day EMA and the relative strength index in the positive zone suggest an advantage to the bulls. If they can push the price above the wedge, the ETH/USD pair could rally to $488.134.\par \par \uc2 A breakout of this resistance could resume the uptrend with the next target at $520 and then $550.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  attempted to break out of the range on Nov. 7 but the bears pushed the price right back in. The bulls are currently attempting to defend the moving averages. If they succeed, another attempt to push the price above $0.26 is likely.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7b50b13a-04c2-4d0d-a97d-e97f2ab8aebd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains above $0.26 for a day, the XRP/USD pair could start a new uptrend with the first target objective at $0.30.\par \par \uc2 However, the flat moving averages and the RSI near the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. If the price slips below the moving averages, the pair could remain range-bound between $0.26 and $0.2295 for the next few days.\par \par \uc2 A break below the $0.2295 to $0.219712 support zone will tilt the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) broke above $272 for the past two days but could not sustain the higher levels. The repeated price rejection shows that the bears are aggressively defending the $272 to $280 resistance zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/58976808-33d8-4947-b5fe-2dc16d471a77.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($257), the BCH/USD pair could drop to $242 and then to $231. Such a move will indicate the possibility of a range-bound action between $231 and $280 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone suggest a minor advantage to the bulls. If the bulls can push the price above the overhead resistance zone, a rally to $300 and then to $326.30 is possible.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls tried to propel Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) above the $13.28 resistance on Nov. 7 but failed. However, the positive thing is that the altcoin bounced off the 20-day EMA ($11.46) and the bulls are again trying to push the price above the overhead resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/0ebce3dc-3cd1-4bd4-b25b-a5df6aad8229.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  inverse head and shoulders pattern that has a target objective of $19.2731. The 20-day EMA ($11.46) has started to turn up gradually and the RSI is in the positive territory, which suggests a minor advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 However, if the price again turns down from the overhead resistance, the bears will try to sink the LINK/USD pair below the moving averages. If they succeed, a drop to $9.7665 is possible.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) is stuck between $32 and $25.6652 for the past few days. The bulls attempted to push the price above the moving averages on Nov. 7 but they failed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f9098693-32a2-4a34-8057-8c64743cfb6f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($28) and the RSI in negative territory suggest that bears have the upper hand. If the price sustains below the moving averages, a drop to $25.6652 is possible.\par \par \uc2 A bounce off this support could extend the stay inside the range for a few more days while a break below it could start a new downtrend.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the BNB/USD pair turns up from the current levels and breaks above $30. Such a move could result in a rally to $32.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) once again turned down from the stiff overhead resistance of $64 on Nov. 7. Barring the breakout on Aug. 17, the price has turned down from this resistance on three occasions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/158d0c60-4d8e-47f4-8de3-5af648bf2a35.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The RSI is forming a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence, which suggests that the momentum may be weakening.\par \par \uc2 If the LTC/USD pair turns down from the current levels or the overhead resistance and plummets below the 20-day EMA ($56), it will increase the possibility of a drop to the 50-day SMA ($50).\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above $64. If they succeed, a rally to $68.9008 is possible.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) is currently trading inside a small range that has resistance at $4.95 and support at $3.80. The price turned down from $4.8586 on Nov. 7, which shows that the bears are aggressively defending this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/4edf163b-9db0-4925-99b9-93d58bd1a24c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls are trying to keep the price above the moving averages and the RSI has also taken support at the 50 level. If the RSI can break out of the downtrend line, it will indicate an advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 If buyers can push the price above $4.95, a rally to $5.5899 is likely. The bears may again defend this level aggressively but if the bulls can thrust the price above it, a new uptrend could begin.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) turned down from the $0.1142241 resistance on Nov. 7, which shows that the bears are aggressively defending this level. However, the positive thing is that the bulls have not allowed the price to dip below the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/def2c6ee-b630-4f33-bf59-7414d743cc18.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The strong rebound off the moving averages on Nov. 8 shows that the sentiment is to buy the dips. The bulls will again attempt to push the price above the overhead resistance. If they can pull it off, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair could rally to $0.128 and then to $0.1445.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price again turns down from $0.1142241, then the range-bound action may continue for a few more days. A break below the moving averages will signal weakness and the bears will then try to sink the pair below $0.0893.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) continues to trade inside the broad range of $146 to $181. The price has been oscillating above and below the moving averages for the past three days, which shows that traders are undecided about the next move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/43562f6f-bcfe-49d8-824c-bdcfac00ca82.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI close to the halfway mark suggest a balance between supply and demand. If the price sustains below the moving averages, the bears will try to sink the BSV/USD pair to the critical support at $146.\par \par \uc2 A rebound off this level could extend the range-bound action for a few more days. The trend will shift in favor of the bulls if they can push the price above the overhead resistance at $181.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvZDNlZTA5ZjktZTMyMi00YjUyLTgwNzItZTM4NTY2NGM5MWI3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201109egb9000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/6: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BNB, LTC, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,804 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price looks slightly overextended in the short-term and may take a break while altcoins play catch-up.\par \par \uc2 The United States Federal Reserve Chair Jerome Powell recently said that additional fiscal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fed-calling-for-more-stimulus-is-code-for-buy-bitcoin-says-winklevoss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stimulus}}}\uc2  could result in a stronger recovery. He also emphasized that the Fed had enough tools to support the economy.\par \par \uc2 After the winner of the U.S. election is announced, the focus of lawmakers could shift to the next stimulus package. However, additional money printing will only worsen the existing national debt which is currently at $27.2 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Even though a new round of stimulus measures may be required in the short-term to reduce the impact of the economic crisis caused by the COVID-19 pandemic, analysts believe that the Fed may not be able to roll back the measures in the future.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/695e1b25-37b5-4ea0-acb2-3ccfe3f7eee8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 For this reason, apprehensive institutional investors have been hedging their portfolio with gold and a few others like billionaire hedge fund manager Paul Tudor Jones have advocated buying Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Galaxy Digital CEO and investor Mike Novogratz believes that Bitcoin is in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/extreme-greed-and-fomo-taking-hold-as-btc-nudges-16k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bull phase}}}\uc2 . Hence, he recently advised Bitcoin HODLers to sit on their hands and lock away their phones to counter the emotion to book profits after the recent rally.\par \par \uc2 While long-term investors could HODL their positions, short-term traders will have to be alert lest they may give back a large part of their unrealized gains.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to see whether the rally has topped out or if it can extend further.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) closed above $14,000 on Nov. 4 and followed the move with a strong rally on Nov. 5. The price reached an intraday high of $15,956.26 today, which is currently acting as a resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f9f78b39-baad-4ae6-afd1-cf1e2defb16c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the trend is clearly in favor of the bulls and any dip is likely to be viewed as a buying opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Although the relative strength index has invalidated the negative divergence, it has risen deep into the overbought territory, which suggests that a few days of consolidation or a correction may be around the corner.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls buy the next dip to $14,000, it will suggest that the previous resistance has flipped to support and this level may act as a floor during future declines.\par \par \uc2 Sometimes, during a buying frenzy, the RSI can remain deeply overbought for a long time. Hence, if the bulls can push the price above $16,000, a move to the $17,000\u8211\'20\'13$17,200 resistance zone is possible. This is the final hurdle before a shot at the all-time highs.\par \par \uc2 However, vertical rallies rarely sustain and they usually end with sharp declines. Hence, traders should exercise caution even if the uptrend continues.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the BTC/USD pair turns down and plummets below the $14,000 support.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) picked up momentum after the bulls pushed the price above the downtrend line on Nov. 4. The upsloping 20-day EMA ($395) and the RSI close to the overbought zone suggest that bulls are in control.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/8b6c2a79-a718-4901-bb80-16cad713900c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The next target on the upside is $450 and if the bulls can push the price above this resistance, the ETH/USD pair may reach $488.134. Even if the bears offer resistance at $450, the bulls are likely to buy the dips as the sentiment has turned positive.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break below the 20-day EMA and the advantage will turn in favor of the bears if the 50-day SMA ($374) cracks.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  has largely been range-bound between $0.2295 and $0.26 for the past few weeks. The failure of the bears to break below the range on Nov. 3 attracted buyers who have pushed the price to the resistance of the range.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/90ac8d99-36b4-4c21-bd3e-2f190babc4e3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push and sustain the price above $0.26, the XRP/USD pair could start a new uptrend that may result in a rally to $0.303746. The RSI has risen above 60 for the first time since August, which suggests that the bulls are making a strong comeback.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair turns down from the current levels or fails to sustain above $0.26, then a few more days of range-bound action is likely. The trend will turn in favor of the bears if the pair plummets below the $0.2295 to $0.219712 support zone.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound off the $231.93 support has reached the 20-day EMA ($255) where the bears may offer resistance. If Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) turns down from the current levels, the bears will again try to sink the price below $231.93.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/aed98360-7d1a-417f-95b7-93131ffb0c1e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bulls push the price above the 20-day EMA, the BCH/USD pair could rise to the overhead resistance zone at $272 to $280.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI has risen to the midpoint, which suggests a possible range-bound action in the near term.\par \par \uc2 A breakout of $280 could signal the start of an up-move that may rise to $326 while a break below $231.93 could result in a fall to $200.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The long tails on the candlesticks of the past three days show that the bulls accumulated on dips below the uptrend line. They have currently pushed Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) above the downtrend line, which suggests that the correction may be over.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/603fd6f6-3d01-4339-91db-1ed1c426dc62.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now try to push the price to the next overhead resistance at $13.28. A breakout and close above this resistance could complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  inverse head and shoulders pattern.\par \par \uc2 However, the flat moving averages and the RSI just above 55 suggest a range-bound action in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 This view will be invalidated if the LINK/USD pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below $9.7665.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) reversed direction from $25.6652 on Nov. 4 and the bulls are currently trying to sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($28.83). This move suggests that the bears are losing their grip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/978eaecc-fd25-42af-b5d7-cb59cf21da00.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains above the moving averages, the bulls will try to push the BNB/USD pair to the overhead resistance at $32.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair turns down from the current levels, the bears will once again attempt to break the $25.6652 support.\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI close to the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. This could result in a few more days of range-bound action between $25.6652 and $32.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The successful retest of the breakout level of the inverse head and shoulders pattern on Nov. 3 and 4 attracted strong buying from the bulls who have pushed \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) above $60.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/bc5e748d-5ba4-4f0d-9e1a-ddef0c8ae212.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is close to the overbought zone, which suggests that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls sustain the momentum and drive the price above $64, the LTC/USD pair could rally to $68.9008.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are unlikely to give up easily. They are currently attempting to stall the up-move at $64 but unless they pull the price back below $60, the advantage will remain with the bulls.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bears to sink Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) below $3.80 on Nov. 3 and 4 attracted buying and the bulls have pushed the price above the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/4f845d73-851a-4646-afac-cdb7a89eb438.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The DOT/USD pair is currently range-bound between $3.80 and $4.95. If the bulls can push the price above $4.6112, the pair may attempt to break above $4.95. If that happens, then a rally to $5.5899 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are flat and the RSI has risen into the positive territory, which suggests a minor advantage to the bulls. However, if the price turns down from $4.6112 or $4.95, the pair may extend its stay inside the range for a few more days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound off the $0.0893 support picked up momentum after the bulls pushed Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above the moving averages. The altcoin is currently attempting to rally to the overhead resistance at $0.1142241.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/3a0f709a-d492-4b70-bb15-77c72b06923c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the overhead resistance, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair could remain range-bound between $0.0893 and $0.1142241 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 However, the flat moving averages and the RSI above 60 suggest that the bulls are attempting a comeback. If the buyers can push the price above $0.1142241, a rally to $0.128 and then to $0.1445 is possible.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and plummets below $0.0893.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) on dips to the $146.20 support on Nov. 3 and 4 as seen from the long tails on the candlesticks. The rebound picked momentum on Nov. 5 and the altcoin has currently risen above the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/92e000c5-5177-414c-be9e-d6705d63f16e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can sustain the price above the moving averages, the BSV/USD pair could rally to $180.63. The bears may defend this level aggressively as the pair had reversed direction from this resistance on three previous occasions.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are flat and the RSI has risen to the midpoint, which suggests that the range-bound action is likely to continue for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, a trending move could start if the bulls push and sustain the price above $180.63 or the bears sink the pair below the $146.20 to $135 support zone.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvMmRmOTcwNzYtYjg0Yi00ZWM1LWFlYmMtOTQ3YmRlOTg0ZDZjLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201106egb6000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/4: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BNB, LTC, DOT,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,812 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 After reaching a new 2020 high, Bitcoin traders are fighting to flip $14,100 to support and Ethereum is attempting to do the same to the $400 level.\par \par \uc2 Today Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price briefly pushed through the $14,100 resistance to achieve a new 2020 high at $14,259 before pulling back to retest $14,100 as support.\par \par \uc2 Although this level represents a critical resistance, data suggests that Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-whales-tread-water-and-hodl-despite-recent-btc-price-drop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whales}}}\uc2  are not closing their positions in a hurry as they expect the current rally to continue. This strong show of confidence is occurring even as there is heightened uncertainty over the result of the U.S. presidential election shows that market participants expect Bitcoin price to move higher regardless of who wins the election.\par \par \uc2 Another \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sign for Bitcoin is the record {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-trust-sees-largest-ever-weekly-inflow-nears-500k-btc-in-total"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflow of $215 million}}}\uc2  into \uc2 Grayscale Bitcoin Trust\uc2  last week. This shows that along with the whales, institutional investors are also \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the prospects of Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 If investors continue to pour money into Grayscale at the current rate, the fund may hold about 2.7% of Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s circulating supply in approximately three weeks.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/88931a40-4263-408c-a3f9-b82e3a5da306.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 During the 2017 bull market, the main driver of Bitcoin price action was the spot market. However, since then, crypto {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-derivatives-volume-more-than-triples-spot-trading"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 derivatives volumes}}}\uc2  have surged, according to Kraken\u8217\'20\'19s November report.\par \par \uc2 The spot volumes hit a high of $570 billion in Q1 2018 but dropped off \u8220\'20\'1Cto a low of $104 billion nearly two years later,\u8221\'20\'1D but \u8220\'20\'1Cderivatives notional volume exploded from below $6B in Q2 2017 to over $1.7T by Q3 2020," the report added.\par \par \uc2 While data suggest greater participation by the professional traders and institutional investors, do the technicals project further upside for Bitcoin and altcoins?\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears could not even sink Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) to the 20-day exponential moving average ($13,057) in the past few days, which showed that the bulls were in no hurry to book profits. This could have attracted another round of buying that has pushed the price to a new 2020 high at $14,259 levels today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/a41153c7-da57-4de3-a876-1a79bfb413ac.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the relative strength index in the overbought zone suggest that the bulls are in control. If they can sustain the price above $14,102, the next leg of the up-move is likely to begin. The next major resistance is close to $16,200.\par \par \uc2 However, the RSI is still showing signs of negative divergence, which usually acts as a reliable warning sign that the momentum may be weakening. But in a strong uptrend, the divergence may turn out to be a fake signal unless the price turns lower.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price turns down from the current levels and the BTC/USD pair plummets below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 Such a move will suggest that the bears are attempting a comeback and they are likely to gain strength if the pair dips below the $12,460 support.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls bought the dip to the uptrend line on Nov. 3 and have followed it up with a breakout of the downtrend line and the $395 resistance today. This suggests that the short-term correction in Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) could be over.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/9b500321-10b0-4f4b-a738-4bc865318f22.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($388) has started to turn up and the RSI has jumped into positive territory, which suggests that bulls have the upper hand. If they can push the ETH/USD pair above $420, the rally may extend to $450 and then to $488.134.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels or the overhead resistance and drops below the 50-day simple moving average ($372).\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls again purchased the dip to the $0.2295 support on Nov. 3 but they could not propel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above the moving averages. This suggests that the bears are aggressively defending this resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/747bb920-b2bf-4992-9da4-64268790e3da.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.244) and the RSI in the negative territory suggest that the bears are in control.\par \par \uc2 If they can sink the price below $0.2295, the XRP/USD pair could drop to $0.219712. A break below this support may resume the downtrend, with the next support at $0.19.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair rebounds off the current levels and rises above the moving averages, then a few more days of range-bound action is likely.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) plunged to $231.93 on Nov. 3 but the bulls purchased this dip as seen from the long tail on the candlestick. Today again, the buyers stepped in and bought the decline to $230.90.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/d5620a64-b563-4023-9f61-a507f0648f7c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This strong rebound suggests that the bulls are attempting to defend the $231.93 support aggressively. However, the downsloping 20-day EMA ($255) and the RSI below 42 suggest that bears are in command.\par \par \uc2 Hence, the bears are likely to sell on rallies to the 20-day EMA. If the BCH/USD pair turns down from the current levels or the overhead resistance and plummets below $231.93, the decline could extend to $210 and then to $200.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the pair picks up momentum and rises above the 20-day EMA. If that happens, the pair could again rally to the $272 to $280 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) broke below the uptrend line today but the bulls purchased the dip to the $9.7665 support. However, the bears will try to stall the pullback at the 20-day EMA ($11) and then at $11.199.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/bcd9febc-2eb6-4d37-b3ad-363698a871b0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping down and the RSI has slipped below 44, which suggests that bears have the upper hand. If the bears can sink the price below $9.7665, the LINK/USD pair could drop to $8.3817 and then to $6.90.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bulls build upon the current bounce and push the price above $11.199. Such a move will increase the possibility of a rally to $13.28.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) closed below $28.43 on Nov. 2, which completed a double top pattern. This setup has a target objective of $24.86 but the bulls are currently attempting to defend the support at $25.6652.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6b2d1c5a-2008-4314-8859-6dfb9cb8d129.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the downsloping 20-day EMA ($28) and the RSI below 37, suggest that the path of least resistance is to the downside. If the bears sink the price below $25.6652, the down-move could resume, with the next major support at $22.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bulls buy the current dip and push the BNB/USD pair back above $28.43. Such a move will open up the possibility of a rally to $32.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls aggressively purchased \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) on dips to $51.2027 on Nov. 3 and have again bought the dip to $51.6109 today, as seen from the long tails on the candlesticks. This suggests that the bulls are defending the $52.36 to $51 support zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/b4e7f907-726a-4e6e-a8b6-e9d66ca2455a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the buyers can sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($53), a rally to $56.50 is possible. However, the flat 20-day EMA and the RSI just above the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 If the LTC/USD pair turns down from the current levels, the bears will again try to sink the price below the support zone. If they succeed, the selling may intensify and the pair could drop to the next support at $46.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears are attempting to sink Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) below $3.80. If they can do that, the altcoin could drop to the critical support at $3.5321. A break below this support could start a new downtrend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f740a08c-d33a-44a6-bd59-3fabc6557a48.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping down and the RSI continues to trade in the negative zone, which suggests that the bears are in control. On a break below $3.5321, the decline could extend to $2.60 and then to $2.00.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bulls defend the $3.80 to $3.5321 support zone and push the price above the moving averages. Such a move could keep the DOT/USD pair range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The long tail on the Nov. 3 candlestick shows that the bulls are buying Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) on dips to $0.0893, but today\u8217\'20\'19s price action suggests that they are not able to sustain the momentum at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/5b0ef750-c044-45d0-9dea-6232a857421f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.0990) and the RSI in the negative zone suggest that the bears have the upper hand. Hence, they may attempt to sell the pullback to the 20-day EMA. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair breaks below $0.0893, it could drop to $0.0755701.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the bulls can push the price above the moving averages. In such a case, a move to $0.104044 and then to $0.1142241 is possible.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) bounced off $145.20 on Nov. 3 and the bulls are again attempting a rebound off the $146.12 level today. This suggests that the bulls are accumulating on dips to the $146.20 to $135 support zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/655892f7-57eb-4e6c-9d92-3a1772da711f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, unless the bulls push the price back above the uptrend line and the moving averages within the next few days, the bears will again try to sink the BSV/USD pair below the support zone.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the pair could start a new downtrend that could result in a decline to $100. The downsloping 20-day EMA ($164) and the RSI in the negative territory suggest that the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvMzA2MzEzYWMtYTAyNy00ZmI2LWE3MDctOGFhMjgxMGY2Yzc5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201104egb4000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin price\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/2: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BNB, LTC, DOT, BSV,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,805 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A minor correction in Bitcoin to $12,500 will not turn it \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  but most altcoins are threatening to break below their critical support levels and start a new downtrend\par \par \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s central bank governor Yi Gang has said that the nation\u8217\'20\'19s digital yuan pilot projects have processed transactions worth over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/china-s-digital-yuan-pilots-have-processed-300m-so-far-says-pboc-head"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $299 million}}}\uc2  without any major problems. This suggests that China is much ahead of its competitors in developing and studying the central bank digital currency (CBDC).\par \par \uc2 However, the \uc2 European Central Bank\uc2  does not want to be left behind. European Central Bank President Christine Lagarde has invited comments from the public on whether they \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be happy to use a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/christine-lagarde-invites-public-comments-on-eurozone-cbdc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 digital Euro}}}\uc2  just in the way they use a Euro coin or a Euro banknote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another central bank that is trying to keep pace is the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 . The central bank has partnered with banks, financial institutions and software companies to study the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/reserve-bank-of-australia-forms-partnerships-to-develop-cbdc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 implications of a CBDC}}}\uc2  for efficiency, risk management and innovation in wholesale financial market transactions,\u8221\'20\'1D said RBA Assistant Governor \uc2 Michele Bullock\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The news of several nations contemplating the launch of a CBDC is a long-term positive but this news may not affect the short-term price action, which is dictated by market sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out whether the sentiment is to buy the dips or sell the rallies.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) failure to rise and sustain above the $13,973.50 overhead resistance in the past few days could have attracted profit booking from some short-term traders and shorting by aggressive bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6649d59e-d5e8-444a-a600-3a75b6912679.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the positive sign is that the bulls are not allowing the bears to have their way. The long tail on the candlestick suggests buying at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 If the BTC/USD pair rises from the current levels, then the bulls will make one more attempt to drive the price above the $13,973.50\u8211\'20\'13$14,101.91 resistance zone. If they succeed, the uptrend could resume.\par \par \uc2 Although both the moving averages are sloping up, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence on the relative strength index suggests that the momentum has weakened. A break below the 20-day exponential moving average ($12,819) will be the first sign of strength for the bears.\par \par \uc2 If the bears can capitalize on this strength and sink the pair below $12,460, then a deeper correction to the 50-day simple moving average ($11,567) is possible.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls had pushed Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) above the downtrend line today but they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-price-faces-a-potential-30-correction-after-failing-to-break-400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could not sustain the higher levels}}}\uc2 . This suggests that the bears are selling on minor rallies. The bears have currently dragged the price back to the 20-day EMA ($386).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/ec328c1b-e70e-4625-a8de-e20df41692f0.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A break and close below the 20-day EMA could drag the price to the uptrend line. The 50-day SMA ($371) is close to this support, hence, the bulls are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 If the ETH/USD pair rebounds off the uptrend line, the bulls will once again try to propel the price above the downtrend line and the $405 overhead resistance. If they succeed, it will increase the possibility of a rally to $420 and then to $450.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bears sink the price below the uptrend line, a fall to $360 and then to $333 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI close to the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. This suggests an equal opportunity for the bulls and the bears in tilting the advantage in their favor.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound from the $0.2295 support in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  hit a barrier at the moving averages and the price has turned down from there. The bears are currently attempting to sink the altcoin below the $0.2295\u8211\'20\'13$0.219712 support zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7051a8f9-b56a-4cd3-a12e-2286906d9cd0.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the XRP/USD pair could start a new downtrend that may reach $0.19. The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.24) and the RSI below 38 suggest that the bears are in control.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls can defend the support zone and push the pair back above the moving averages, it will suggest accumulation at lower levels. In such a case, the pair may remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) has once again turned down from the $272 resistance and the bears are currently attempting to pull the price below the 20-day EMA ($258.58) and the immediate support at $253.14.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/11b44cc7-eacd-4f47-a966-79fe44199bfc.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears manage to do that, the BCH/USD pair could drop to the next support at the 50-day SMA ($240.57).\par \par \uc2 Although the moving averages are still sloping up gradually, the RSI has broken down from a symmetrical triangle and has dropped close to the midpoint. This suggests that the bears are attempting to make a comeback.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair bounces off the 20-day EMA and breaks above the $272\u8211\'20\'13$280 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($11.21) on Nov. 1 but they could not build upon this momentum. Today, the price has again dipped back below the 20-day EMA and the bears are currently attempting to break the support at the 50-day SMA ($10.51).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/3cb315cc-6eb7-402b-825d-0bd660930a49.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A breakdown and close below the uptrend line will be the first sign that the bears are back in action. There is minor support at $9.7665 but if the bears can sink the price below it, a drop to $8.3817 will be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the LINK/USD pair turns up from the current levels or bounces off the uptrend line and rises above $12. Such a move could result in a rally to $13.28.\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI below the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. Hence, neither the bulls nor the bears have a clear advantage.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has been trading near the 50-day SMA ($28) for the past three days, which suggests that the bulls are attempting to defend this support. However, the bears are unlikely to give up their advantage easily.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/a2d64b63-746d-4ac9-8005-9fb1fa881c0e.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 They sold the rally to the 20-day EMA ($29) today and are currently attempting to pull the price below the $28.42\u8211\'20\'13$27.51 support zone. If they can pull it off, the BNB/USD pair could decline to $24.86.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI below 43 suggest that the bears have the upper hand. However, if the bears fail to capitalize on the advantage, the bulls will again try to push the price above the 20-day EMA. If they succeed, the pair could move up to $32.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) has once again turned down from just above the $56.50 level today, which suggests that the bears are defending this resistance. The sellers will now try to sink the altcoin below the $52.36\u8211\'20\'13$51 support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7d8f0599-e46c-4f44-b6ea-1b6c30d9aa5e.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they can do that, then the LTC/USD pair could drop to the 50-day SMA ($49) and if this support also cracks, the decline may extend to $46.\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls are likely to buy the drop to the support zone. The flat 20-day EMA ($53) and the RSI just above the midpoint suggests a range-bound action for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The advantage will tilt in favor of the bulls if they can push and sustain the price above $56.50.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The bounce from the $3.80 support in Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) fizzled out at the 20-day EMA ($4.22). The bears will now try to sink the price below the immediate support at $3.80. If that happens, a drop to $3.5321 will be on the cards.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/3c42fec7-c3d9-48a1-9f6e-0df70817d45e.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI is in the negative territory, which suggests a slight advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 If the bears can sink the price below $3.5321, the DOT/USD pair may start a new downtrend that could reach $2.60 and then $2.0.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bulls defend the $3.80\u8211\'20\'13$3.5321 support zone, the pair may remain range-bound between $3.5321 and $4.6112 for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to push Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($166) in the past three days shows a lack of demand at higher levels. This has attracted selling by the bears who are currently attempting to sink the price below the uptrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7d245b5f-bd5d-44ef-bd94-48767d38393d.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the BSV/USD pair could drop to the $146.20\u8211\'20\'13$135 support zone. A breakdown of this zone could result in panic selling that may start a new downtrend. The next support on the downside is at $100.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls defend the support zone, the pair could remain range-bound between $146.20\u8211\'20\'13$180.63 for a few more days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound from the $0.0893 support in Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has turned down from the 20-day EMA ($0.10). This is a negative sign as it shows that the bears are selling on rallies.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below $0.0893, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair could drop to the critical support at $0.07555701. The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative territory suggest that the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair again rebounds off the $0.0893 support, it will suggest that bulls are accumulating closer to this level. A break above $0.104044 will be the first sign that the bulls are attempting a comeback.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvZmM0NWE5M2YtYjlkOC00Njc3LTg3NWMtYTM0M2ZkM2NiYWNkLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201102egb2000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin price\par \b \uc2 Top 5 cryptocurrencies to watch this week: BTC, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BCH, LINK\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,590 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin could pick up momentum above $14,000 but altcoins may continue to struggle in the short-term\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has rallied about 90% year-to-date and has risen close to 191% from its March lows. The rise has been gradual without much fanfare, which suggests that crypto believers are the ones who have been buying in 2020.\par \par \uc2 October\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-monthly-candle-closes-above-13k-for-the-first-time-since-2017"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monthly close}}}\uc2  at $13,798.99 is the highest ever, surpassing the December 2017 close at $13,789.68. The strong performance of Bitcoin may now attract the momentum players and the speculators who look to benefit from the strength.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6f6e38a1-06ce-4ddc-9136-2684def79a64.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market weekly performance data. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 If that happens, then Bitcoin could pick up momentum and surprise investors to the upside. This could result in traders selling their altcoins to invest in Bitcoin. Hence, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-bitcoin-price-and-volume-rising-together-is-bad-news-for-ethereum-altseason"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 altseason looks to be over}}}\uc2  in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 Three of the top-five cryptocurrencies analyzed today may offer a trading opportunity to the upside while the other two may continue to decline further. Let\u8217\'20\'19s watch the critical levels that may indicate the start of a trending move.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin rose above the $13,973.50 overhead resistance and reached an intraday high of $14,101.91 on Oct. 31. Although the bulls failed to sustain the price above the resistance, they have not given up much ground to the downside.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/dd8750dd-cfbf-4a65-865c-5d1493112293.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This suggests that traders are not closing their positions in a hurry because they expect another attempt by the bulls to propel the price above the resistance.\par \par \uc2 Both the 10-day exponential moving average ($13,309) and the 50-day simple moving average ($11,505) are sloping up and the relative strength index is in the overbought territory. This suggests that the bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 If the BTC/USD pair closes above $14,000, the next leg of the uptrend could begin that can reach $16,500.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls again fail to sustain the price above $14,000, then the short-term traders may dump their positions and the bears could initiate short positions. A break below the 10-day EMA will be the first sign that the momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 The bears are likely to gain an upper hand if the pair drops and sustains below the critical support at $12,460.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/84187698-3014-4d54-92e8-0719cbe77773.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The pair is currently attempting to hold above the 10-EMA. If that happens and the bulls succeed in pushing the price above the $13,973.50\u8211\'20\'13$14,101.92 resistance zone, a new uptrend is likely.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence on the RSI suggests that the upside momentum is weakening. If the sellers can sink the pair below the 10-EMA, a drop to the 50-SMA and then to $13,000 will be on the cards. The strong support in the $12,750\u8211\'20\'13$13,000 zone could attract buyers.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke below the $28.50 support on Oct. 30 but managed to bounce from the intraday lows and close above $28.50. However, the doji candlestick pattern on Oct. 31 suggested indecision among the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/65bc857a-8040-43d8-9567-47b445dbee50.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bears are currently attempting to resolve the indecision to the downside and gain the upper hand. If the BNB/USD pair breaks and closes below $27.50, it will increase the possibility of a drop to $24.86.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 10-day EMA ($29.47) and the RSI in the negative zone suggests that the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price reverses direction and rises above $28.50, then it will suggest a few more days of consolidation.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/bf2f4272-2fbd-4572-9329-76395f1c010c.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the recovery from $27.5111 is facing stiff resistance at the 10-EMA. A break below $28 could challenge the $27.50 support, which if broken, the next stop could be $26.50.\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping down and the RSI is close to the oversold zone, suggesting an advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 This view will be invalidated if the pair turns around and rises above $29. Such a move will suggest accumulation at lower levels and will increase the possibility of a rise to $30.50.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) broke below the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  rising wedge pattern on Oct. 26 and plunged to the $0.0891 support. The bulls are currently attempting to defend the support and push the price above the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/6aa2f509-32d5-4565-bb5c-6b62d1a54920.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the downsloping 10-day EMA ($0.988) and the RSI below 43 suggest that bears are in control. Therefore, the bounce is likely to face stiff resistance at the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair turns down from this resistance, the bears will again try to break the $0.0891 support. Such a move will open the gates for a decline to the next support at $0.0755.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bulls can push and sustain the price above the moving averages. Such a move could result in a rally to $0.11.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/b9e2e603-4744-4b7b-9f15-31bdce474318.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls have pushed the price above the 10-EMA on the 4-hour chart. The pair could now move up to the 50-SMA where bears may again step in and sell.\par \par \uc2 Although the 50-SMA is still sloping down, the 10-EMA is attempting to turn up and the RSI has risen to the midpoint, which suggests that the selling pressure has reduced in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair turns down from the current levels or the 50-SMA, the bears will once again try to sink the price below the $0.0891 support. If they succeed, the next leg of the down move could begin.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) has formed a symmetrical triangle, which usually acts as a continuation pattern. However, as this setup suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears, it is better to wait for the price to break above the triangle before taking a directional bet.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/f583f75c-d4c4-4e7f-98a5-471950bf8b92.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is above 59, which suggests that the bulls have the upper hand. If the bulls can push and sustain the price above the triangle, the BCH/USD pair could move up to $280 and then to $296.87.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price breaks below the triangle, the BCH/USD pair could drop to the critical support at $242. The 50-day SMA ($239) is placed just below this support, hence, the bulls may buy a drop to this zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/b4606225-a214-44f5-a6e9-05a9a70aa5ea.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls had pushed the price above the resistance line of the symmetrical triangle but they could not sustain the higher levels and the bears have dragged the price back into the triangle.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair bounces off the 50-SMA or the 10-EMA, the bulls will make one more attempt to propel the price above the triangle. If they succeed, the momentum could pick up and a rally to $280 is likely.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be negated if the price breaks below the moving averages and drops below the symmetrical triangle.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) has been trading inside an ascending channel for the past few days. Although the pace of rise has been slow, the altcoin has been making successive higher highs and higher lows.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/4f3ca8c2-7c2e-43cb-abb8-b698566c2d4f.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The LINK/USD pair is currently correcting after turning down from the overhead resistance at $13. Both moving averages have flattened out and the RSI is close to the midpoint, suggesting a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 The bulls are likely to purchase the drop to the support line of the channel. If the price rebounds off this support with strength, the bulls may again attempt to push the pair above $13.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the bears sink the price below the channel. Such a move could drag the price down to $8.3817 and below that to $7.2869.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-11/7eafe101-76cd-441a-ba7e-eb1797bacfd1.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD 4-hour chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to defend the uptrend line. If they can push the price above the downtrend line, the pair could start its journey towards $13.\par \par \uc2 However, the 10-EMA has flattened out and the RSI has been trading in the negative territory, which suggests that bears are attempting a comeback in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 If the bears can sink the price below the uptrend line, the pair could drop to the support line of the channel. The bulls will attempt to defend this support and if they succeed, the pair may rise to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTEvMDg4ZGY0ODYtOWU4Ny00N2ZkLTllZTItOGJhMmVkOTk4MWI2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201101egb10008f\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/30: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BNB, DOT, LTC, BSV,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,766 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s consolidation near a key overhead resistance is a sign of strength but the chart structure of most altcoins has weakened.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) dominance has risen from about 56% in early September to above 63%. This suggests that the market participants may be rotating their investments out of altcoins to buy Bitcoin. Due to this, several altcoins have either corrected or formed a range.\par \par \uc2 While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-suddenly-slides-4-as-bofa-predicts-a-20-stock-market-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legacy markets}}}\uc2  are keeping a close eye on the U.S. Presidential elections, Grayscale CEO Barry Silbert believes that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/trump-or-biden-bitcoin-wins-regardless-of-us-election-barry-silbert"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price will gain}}}\uc2  irrespective of the result because the next President will continue to print more dollars.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/28db7399-4548-4711-bfe0-60ee722424ab.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Using data from CoinMetrics, \uc2 Twitter\uc2  user Julio Moreno recently highlighted that if Bitcoin could sustain above $10,000 for four more days, it would complete 100 days above this critical level.\par \par \uc2 History suggests that Bitcoin rallies vertically after it completes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-just-4-days-away-from-historically-bullish-10k-price-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 100 days}}}\uc2  above a psychologically significant level. Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s rally from $10 to $100, a 10-fold rise, took only 122 days after it had spent 100 days above $10.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, a move from $100 to $1000 happened in two days, and the rally from $1,000 to $10,000 was completed in 150 days. Therefore, investors are watching to see whether Bitcoin will continue following its precedence or will it chalk a new course.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out the path of least resistance.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The long tail on the candlesticks of the past two days shows that the bulls are accumulating on dips. However, the failure to sustain Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) above $13,600 suggests that the bears are attempting to defend the overhead resistance.\par \par \uc2 After the large range day on Oct. 28, the price action could be subdued for a few days as both the bulls and the bears try to gain an upper hand.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping moving averages and the relative strength index still in the overbought zone suggests that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will again try to push the BTC/USD pair above $13,973.50 and if they succeed, the uptrend could resume.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the index turns down from the current levels and slips below the 20-day exponential moving average ($12,518), the trend could turn in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has broken below the 20-day EMA ($385) today but the bulls are attempting to defend the support at the 50-day simple moving average ($370). The uptrend line is also just below this level, hence, a bounce is likely.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/5bfc0cff-1429-4d93-bb65-ad2b29c2007e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above the downtrend line, the ETH/USD pair may rise to the $420.50 overhead resistance. A break above this level could increase the possibility of a rally to $450 and then to $488.134.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the bears sink the ETH/USD pair below the uptrend line, a drop to $333 and then to $308.392 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI near the midpoint do not indicate an advantage to either the bulls or the bears. Hence, the pair could remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 After failing to sustain above the $0.26\u8211\'20\'13$0.2295 range on Oct. 22, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  has dropped to the support of the range. However, the long tail on the candlestick today suggests that bulls are using this dip to buy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/32141b7a-108c-4d5e-98e4-0d3ab1ba8bd6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 It is difficult to predict the direction of the breakout from the range, hence, it is better to wait for the price to break above or below the range before taking a large bet.\par \par \uc2 In a consolidation phase, the signals from the moving averages are choppy. The oversold levels on the RSI are considered as a buying opportunity and overbought levels are used to book profits because the expectation is that the range-bound action will continue.\par \par \uc2 A trending move could be expected if the bears sink the XRP/USD pair below the $0.2295\u8211\'20\'13$0.219712 support zone, while a break above $0.26 will suggest that the bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The long wick on the candlestick on Oct. 28 shows that bulls booked profits when Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) failed to rise above $280. Although the bulls purchased the dip to the 20-day EMA ($256) on Oct. 29, the price has again slipped today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/bfd57a80-eb2d-4565-8c11-f8daa8122318.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The RSI has broken down from the symmetrical triangle, which suggests that the bears are attempting to make a comeback. If the bears can sink the price below the 20-day EMA, a drop to $242 is possible.\par \par \uc2 This support could attract buying as the 50-day SMA ($238) is just below it. If the BCH/USD pair rebounds off this support, it could remain range-bound between $280\u8211\'20\'13$242 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the pair below the 50-day SMA, a drop to $210 could be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) has broken below the 20-day EMA ($11.21) support and the bears are now attempting to sink the price below the 50-day SMA ($10.58). If the bears succeed, the altcoin could dip to the uptrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/827e89eb-e632-40e4-8bbc-aad32feff750.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A break below the uptrend line could signal an advantage to the bears and open the gates for a possible decline to $8.38 and then $6.90.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the rebound off the current levels or the uptrend line sustains above the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again try to propel the LINK/USD pair above $13.28.\par \par \uc2 However, the flat moving averages and the RSI near the midpoint indicate a balance between supply and demand. This could result in a range-bound action in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The bears are currently attempting to sink and sustain Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) below the $28.43 support. If they succeed, the altcoin will complete a double top pattern that could drag the price down to the target objective of $24.86.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/5bbb2fa4-1cdd-4f95-b1e6-ef1c11713f1d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($29.81) has started to turn down and the RSI has plunged into negative territory, which suggests the bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 However, if the bulls buy the current dip and push the price back above $28.43, the BNB/USD pair could rise to the 20-day EMA where it may face resistance.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from this resistance, it will suggest that the sentiment has turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  and traders are looking to sell on rallies.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bulls can push the price above $32, it will suggest that the bulls are back in control.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) plummeted back below the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders pattern on Oct. 29. This drop has invalidated the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/611670ad-754c-4019-a93e-a39cac233b5f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently trying to find support close to $3.80. If this support cracks, the bears will try to break the $3.5321 support and if they succeed, the DOT/USD pair could start a downtrend that may reach $2.60.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the pair rebounds off the current levels, the pair may again attempt to rise above the moving averages and $4.6112. If that happens, it will suggest that the bulls are accumulating at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The reversal on Oct. 28 attracted further follow up selling on Oct. 29 and \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) broke the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $54.9361. Currently, the bulls are attempting to defend the $52.36 support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/020e30b9-a01f-42f4-9390-b37926b58fe5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the LTC/USD pair could consolidate between $52 and $60 for a few days. The flattening 20-day EMA ($53) and the RSI just above the halfway mark also suggest a few days of range-bound action.\par \par \uc2 This assumption will be invalidated if the bears sink the pair below the $52.36\u8211\'20\'13$51 support. If this happens, the pair could drop to the 50-day SMA ($49) and below that to $46.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) broke below the 20-day EMA ($167) on Oct. 29 and that has been followed by further selling today. Currently, the altcoin has dropped to the uptrend line of the symmetrical triangle.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/188bb82f-648f-469b-b251-ec34287fd5a0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A break below the uptrend line could drag the price down to the $146.20 support where the bulls are likely to step in and buy. A bounce off $146.20 could keep the BSV/USD pair stuck inside the range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI in the negative territory also suggest a balance between supply and demand. This view of a range formation will be invalidated if the bulls push the price above $180.63 or the bears sink the pair below $146.20.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) broke below the 50-day SMA ($0.092) on Oct. 29 and the bears are currently attempting to sink the price below the $0.0893 support. If they succeed, the altcoin may drop to $0.0755701.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/3a64df3a-d74d-4a4f-b9b9-3ca0fecf87a8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.102) and the RSI below 38 indicate that bears are in command.\par \par \uc2 Even if the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair rises from the current levels, the bears will try to sell the bounce to the 20-day EMA. If the pair turns down from this resistance, it will increase the possibility of a break below $0.0893.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bulls can push the pair above $0.1040440. Such a move will suggest accumulation at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTAvNjc1NDNhNmEtZmE4Ny00N2JlLWJiYjItNjA5ZjVmNTEwOTI5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201030egau000e3\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/28: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BNB, DOT, LTC, BSV,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,825 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Altcoins took a serious hit as Bitcoin dropped below $13K today, meanwhile, BTC\u8217\'20\'19s macrostructure remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The equity markets across Europe closed deeply in the red and the U.S. markets are also witnessing intense selling pressure as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2020/10/27/stock-market-futures-open-to-close-news.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investors fear}}}\uc2  a rise in COVID-19 cases could stall the fragile economic recovery. This increasingly negative sentiment has also dragged gold and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) prices lower, while the U.S. dollar currency index has risen.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Bitcoin has largely acted as an uncorrelated asset, barring short periods of time when it has followed the S&P 500 or gold. Therefore, investors should take a l {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/3-reasons-why-bitcoin-price-suddenly-dropping-below-13-000-isn-t-bearish"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 onger-term view}}}\uc2  rather than panicking due to short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/b1465174-a1cb-43d3-adfd-8b684e1f4637.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 A survey by Grayscale has shown that the number of investors who are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-investing-interest-up-19-compared-to-2019-grayscale-report-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 familiar with Bitcoin}}}\uc2  has risen from 53% in 2019 to 62% this year. The poll also showed that about 55% of the respondents were interested in Bitcoin investment products this year, compared to 36% in 2019.\par \par \uc2 With greater participation from both retail and institutional investors, the crypto markets may become less prone to manipulation and that could in turn attract more investments.\par \par \uc2 When an asset enters a correction, knowing the strong support levels can help traders to make a more informed decision. Therefore, let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies in order to spot the critical levels that may attract buyers.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has turned down sharply from just under the critical overhead resistance of $13,973.50, which suggests profit-booking by short-term traders and likely initiation of short positions by the aggressive bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/18ba1883-56ca-4fb6-ade9-78f7f1ef29f0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price closes below $13,041.5, the BTC/USD pair would form a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  engulfing candlestick pattern, which is a warning sign that the trend may be reversing. The first stop on the downside is the 20-day exponential moving average ($12,289).\par \par \uc2 A break below this support will suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has weakened and that could intensify selling, dragging the price to the 50-day simple moving average ($11,238)\par \par \uc2 However, as the moving averages are sloping up and the relative strength index has corrected its overbought levels, the bulls are likely to buy the dips to the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 A strong bounce off this support will suggest that the sentiment is \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  as traders are buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound off the 20-day EMA ($385) on Oct. 26 could not sustain the higher levels on Oct. 27 as the bears sold on recovery. This has dragged Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) below the 20-day EMA today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/329ff6f8-9a66-4fa5-9d1f-ad499267fb1f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bears sustain the price below the 20-day EMA, a drop to the uptrend line is likely. A break below this support could drag the ETH/USD pair to the next support at $333 and then to $308.096.\par \par \uc2 However, if the price recovers from the current levels and rises above the $400\u8211\'20\'13$420 resistance zone, it will signal an advantage to the bulls. Above $420, the pair could start its journey to $450 and then to $488.134.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  continues to trade inside a range as the flat moving averages and the RSI just below the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. If the bears can sink and sustain the price below the 50-day SMA ($0.245), the altcoin could drop to $0.2295.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/a3243518-bad2-437c-af0a-ce62b243bd1c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A break below the $0.2295\u8211\'20\'13$0.2197 support zone could tilt the advantage in favor of the bears. However, if the price rebounds off the support zone, the XRP/USD pair could extend its stay inside the range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the pair rebounds off the 50-day SMA and rises above the $0.26 resistance, it will indicate that bulls are in command. Above $0.26, the pair could start an up-move that may reach $0.30.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 20-day EMA ($256) on Oct. 26 and the bulls are currently trying to propel the price above the overhead resistance at $280. If they can pull it off, the altcoin could rise to $300 and then to $326.30.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/ac44b720-8871-4d80-8a78-d849c509cf3e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 62 suggests that the bulls are in control. However, the RSI has formed a negative divergence and a possible symmetrical triangle.\par \par \uc2 If the RSI breaks above the triangle, it will increase the possibility of an up-move in the BCH/USD pair. Conversely, if the RSI breaks below the triangle, it will suggest the start of a pullback.\par \par \uc2 The failure to drive the price above $280 could attract profit-booking by short-term traders. A break below the 20-day EMA ($256) will signal that the momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 The rebound off the $11.199 support on Oct. 26 was short-lived as the bulls could not sustain the higher levels on Oct. 27. The bears have jumped on this opportunity and are currently attempting to sink Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) back below $11.199.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/7dc045b7-9fd4-4328-9cf3-3b6e63c2862a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the LINK/USD pair could drop to the trendline. A break below the trendline could signal an advantage to the bears that may result in a fall to $8.38.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the pair rebounds off the current levels, the bulls will once again try to push the price above $13.28 and extend the recovery to $18.\par \par \uc2 The indicators are not giving any clear signals as both moving averages have flattened out and the RSI has dropped close to the halfway mark, suggesting a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) above the $32 resistance on Oct. 27 but could not sustain the higher levels. This shows that the bears are defending the zone between $32\u8211\'20\'13$33.3888.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/1703da27-11c0-4709-9866-b507f85dc2c3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The failure to sustain above $32 could have attracted profit booking from the short-term traders. If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($29.94), the BNB/USD pair may drop to the 50-day SMA ($28.24).\par \par \uc2 However, the trend remains up as both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is in the positive territory. Therefore, the bulls may attempt to buy on dips to the moving averages. The uptrend will resume on a close above $33.3888.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the bears sink the price below the 50-day SMA, it may increase the possibility of a deeper correction to $26 and then 22.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) above the $4.6112 resistance on Oct. 26 but the sellers were in no mood to relent and they aggressively defended the overhead resistance at $5 on Oct. 27.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/84e00b71-aa3a-461b-875f-9f5df2d98a2f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The failure to sustain above $4.6112 has again dragged the price down to the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders pattern.\par \par \uc2 If the DOT/USD pair rebounds off this support, the bulls will again try to propel the price above $5 and reach the overhead resistance at $5.5899.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bears sink the price below the neckline, the pair may again drop to $3.5321. A bounce off this support could keep the pair range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $54.9361 on Oct. 26, which showed that the bulls were not willing to wait for lower levels to buy as they expected the uptrend to resume.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/68805988-08d3-418e-88a6-aeda603ca0d8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Although the bulls had pushed the LTC/USD pair above $60 today, they could not sustain the higher levels. This attracted aggressive selling from short-term traders and the price again dropped to the 38.2% retracement level.\par \par \uc2 If the bears can sink the pair below $54.9361, the correction may extend to $53.2915 and then to $51.\par \par \uc2 However, if the pair again rebounds off $54.9361, a few days of range-bound action is possible. The pair is likely to pick up momentum after the price sustains above $60.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip to the breakout level of the symmetrical triangle on Oct. 26 but they could not push Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) above the $180\u8211\'20\'13$185.14 overhead resistance zone on Oct. 27 and start a new uptrend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/ce84d9dc-273c-4b05-91ae-13621fc5e8f3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The failure to rise above the overhead resistance could have attracted selling by the short-term bulls and the aggressive bears. As a result, the BSV/USD pair has again dropped down to the 20-day EMA ($168).\par \par \uc2 If the pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again attempt to propel the price above the overhead resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bears sink the price below the moving averages, the pair could may to the uptrend line of the triangle and then to $146.20.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 The long tail on the Oct. 26 candlestick shows that the bulls purchased the dip to the 50-day SMA ($0.098). However, the buyers could not build upon this strength and sustain Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.103) on Oct. 27.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/cf91977b-23d2-4997-b1f0-a7f151bf7520.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This shows that demand dries up at higher levels. The bears pounced on this sign of weakness and resumed their selling today and have managed to sink the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair below the 50-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below this level, the next support is at $0.090 and if this support also gives way, the decline could extend to the critical support at $0.0755701.\par \par \uc2 With the latest fall, the 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI has dipped into the negative zone, indicating an advantage to the bears.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns around from the current levels or the immediate support and rises above $0.104044.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTAvNjY4MTI1NTUtNGVhZC00YWNkLThkOGYtMmM5NDY3MTBhMThkLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201028egas000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/26: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, LINK, BNB, DOT, LTC, BSV,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,686 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins are showing signs of short-term exhaustion, meaning a few days of consolidation could occur.\par \par \uc2 Morgan Creek Digital co-founder {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-decoupling-from-stocks-as-ultimate-safe-haven-anthony-pompliano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anthony Pompliano highlighted data from Santiment, which showed that the 30-day rolling correlation}}}\uc2  between Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and the S&P 500 is 0. Pomp stressed that the lack of correlation shows that Bitcoin is a store of value.\par \par \uc2 Along with that, Bitcoin has also outperformed most traditional asset classes such as gold, the S&P 500, crude oil, and the U.S. dollar since the sector wide crash that took place in March when coronavirus fears reached a peak.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/301e5ae8-6ae0-4da6-9c90-97fcd2a3c09e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Abra Co-founder and CEO Bill Barhydt recently said that \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin is the single best investment opportunity in the world right now\u8221\'20\'1D and he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/abra-ceo-s-portfolio-is-50-bitcoin-as-cash-is-becoming-worthless"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 substantially}}}\uc2  increased his Bitcoin holdings in the past few days. After the recent purchase, about 50% of Barhydt\u8217\'20\'19s total investment portfolio is now held in Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Is Bitcoin likely to resume its uptrend or will it take a pause and consolidate for a few days before starting the next trending move? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to propel Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) above the $13,200\u8211\'20\'13$13,343.66 resistance zone. This suggests that after the initial frenzy, buying has dried up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/a960ab74-7e84-40ad-8782-931977a1fc61.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The failure to sustain above $13,200 could attract profit booking by the short-term traders that may result in a pullback to the $12,460\u8211\'20\'13$12,050 support zone.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping moving averages and the relative strength index in the overbought territory, shows that the bulls are in command. Therefore, the bulls might buy the dip to the 20-day exponential moving average ($12,034).\par \par \uc2 If the BTC/USD pair rebounds sharply from the 20-day EMA, the bulls will make one more attempt to resume the uptrend. If they succeed, a rally to $14,000 is likely.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bears can sink the pair below the 20-day EMA, a fall to the 50-day simple moving average ($11,109) is possible.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 The tight range consolidation of the past three days has resolved the downside. The bears have dragged Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) back below $395 but the bulls are attempting to keep the price above the 20-day EMA ($383).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/7f6a9437-a6ab-44d7-adf0-6ee6650366e8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the ETH/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA and rises above $400, it will suggest strong accumulation at lower levels. A breakout of $420 will signal the possible resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 However, the 20-day EMA is flattening out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, which suggests a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 If the bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the momentum has weakened. A break below the uptrend line may intensify the selling.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to push {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above the $0.26 resistance in the past few days may have attracted profit booking by the short-term traders. The altcoin has broken below the 20-day EMA ($0.249) and is currently attempting to stay above the 50-day SMA ($0.244).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/ee6b8c93-ca3f-45c6-834e-dbe8f8376bdd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the XRP/USD pair rebounds off the 50-day SMA, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above $0.26. If they can pull it off, the pair is likely to pick up momentum and rally to $0.30.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the bears sink the price below the 50-day SMA, the pair could extend its stay inside the $0.2295\u8211\'20\'13$0.26 range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The flattening moving averages and the RSI just below 50 also point to a possible range-bound action in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to propel Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) above the $280 resistance attracted profit booking by the short-term traders. This selling has dragged the price down to the 20-day EMA ($252).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/215b1bab-def6-40e6-976b-7034eccac9c1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the BCH/USD pair rebounds sharply from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest accumulation at lower levels. The bulls will then again try to push the price above the overhead resistance at $280.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the rally may extend to $300 and above it to $326.30. Conversely, if bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, the BCH/USD pair could drop to $242. Such a move will suggest that the pair could remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The RSI has formed a negative divergence, which suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum may be weakening.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) has turned down from close to $13 levels and the bears will now attempt to pull the price back below the $11.8028\u8211\'20\'13$11.1990 support zone. If they succeed, it will suggest that the recent breakout of $11.8028 was a bull trap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/57575b4e-ba15-4543-96e5-084191518f96.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A break below the moving averages could signal further weakness and the trend will turn in favor of the bears if the uptrend line also fails to provide support.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the LINK/USD pair rebounds off the $11.8028-$11.1990 support, it will suggest that the bulls are buying the dips. The bulls will then make one more attempt to propel the pair above $13.28.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the uptrend is likely to pick up momentum with a rally to $15 and then to $17.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) remains in an uptrend and the bulls have held the support at $29.5646 for the past four days. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 57 signals that bulls are in command.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/4e0380d3-aff5-4d42-8db0-ee3f63d827bd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can thrust the BNB/USD pair above the $32\u8211\'20\'13$33.3888 resistance zone, the uptrend may pick up momentum. A breakout of the resistance zone increases the possibility of a retest of the all-time highs.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, the first sign of weakness will be a break below the 20-day EMA ($29.68) and the pair could signal a deeper correction if it sustains below the 50-day SMA ($27.91).\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) broke above the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders pattern on Oct. 24. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup has a target objective of $5.40. The bulls are currently attempting to push and sustain the price above the overhead resistance at $4.6112.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/e50f28d6-fdae-47d6-b750-414f2953bf5b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the buyers can manage to sustain the price above $4.6112, the momentum is likely to pick up. The 20-day EMA ($4.22) has flattened out and the RSI has risen above 59, which suggests that the selling pressure has reduced.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated if the DOT/USD pair turns around from the current levels and plummets below the moving averages. Such a move will suggest that the break above the neckline was a bull trap.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) turned around from the $60 mark as traders booked profits following the sharp gains of the past few days. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 62 suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/e9636366-d223-4c3a-9006-5ce2a163aeca.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The LTC/USD pair has corrected to the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $54.9361 and if this support cracks, a drop to the 50% retracement level of $53.3915 is likely.\par \par \uc2 If the pair bounces from either level, it will suggest buying on dips. In such a case, the bulls will again try to resume the up-move by driving the price above $60. If they succeed, the pair could rally to $64 and then to $68.9008.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears sink the pair below the breakout zone of $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) broke above the symmetrical triangle on Oct. 24 but the bulls could not build up on the strength and push the price above the overhead resistance at $180.63.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/2f88554c-d177-43bf-83d2-a8e31542f29f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 This has resulted in profit booking that has dragged the price close to the 20-day EMA ($167). A break below the moving averages could pull the price down to the uptrend line of the triangle.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the BSV/USD pair rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above $180.63. If they are successful, a rally to $208 and then to $227 is possible.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has broken down of the support line of the rising wedge pattern and the 20-day EMA ($0.10). The bulls are currently attempting to defend the support at the 50-day SMA ($0.099).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/d72c7c85-1bba-46ed-b071-472a1d43b12b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair rebounds off the current levels, the bulls will make one more attempt to drive the price above $0.1142241.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the bears sink the price below the 50-day SMA, a drop to $0.90 and then to $0.755701 is possible.\par \par \uc2 The flat moving averages and the RSI just below 45 suggest that bears have a minor advantage.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTAvZTE3Nzk3M2EtZjhhOS00MTVjLWJkZDEtZDM5MjkxYzM2MjVhLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201026egaq000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin Price\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/23: BTC, ETH, XRP, BCH, BNB, LINK, DOT, LTC,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BSV\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,791 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 October 2020\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2020. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is showing signs of profit booking, resulting in a slight downturn in altcoin prices.\par \par \uc2 PayPal\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crypto announcement acted as a trigger that drove Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price to a new 52-week high. During such news-based events, traders holding short positions are caught off guard and are forced to cover their trades, resulting in the type of short squeeze seen during the Oct. 21 rally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/0114c775-c52a-4027-9fff-e4ef73276e40.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency market weekly performance. Source: Coin360.com\par \par \uc2 However, after this initial burst, the next leg of the uptrend is only possible if demand picks up and the bulls continue to buy at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 Data from Huobi exchange suggests that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/3-key-metrics-and-disinterest-from-pro-traders-hint-at-bitcoin-price-sell-off"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro traders are not convinced that the current rally warrants the opening of long positions}}}\uc2  and Cointelegraph contributor Marcel Pechman explained that this could be a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  signal.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-frenzy-cme-becomes-2nd-biggest-bitcoin-futures-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open interest}}}\uc2  on CME Bitcoin futures paints a different picture. The CME has now become the second biggest Bitcoin futures exchange in terms of open interest, second only to OKEx. This suggests that institutional demand could be picking up.\par \par \uc2 This opposing set of data from Bitcoin futures exchanges only adds to the confusion among traders about the next possible move.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s go a little deep into the psychology of the traders for a better understanding. Institutional investors rarely buy because of FOMO as they are generally more averse to\par \par \uc2 These large traders may wait for the rally to sustain and complete a successful retest of the breakout level before buying.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s take a look at the top-10 cryptocurrencies in order to determine what the technical indicators project.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) broke out and closed above the $12,460 resistance on Oct. 21. This move helped the cryptocurrency notch a new 52-week high, which is a sign of strength.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/85c6ab1d-ab7a-42f0-b00c-1f357790bfdc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average ($11,679) is sloping up and the 50-day simple moving average ($10,943) has also started to rise. This shows that both the short-term and the medium-term trend favors the bulls.\par \par \uc2 However, the rally above $13,000 pushed the relative strength index close to 81, a level which attracted profit booking the last two times it was reached.\par \par \uc2 The BTC/USD pair is facing selling above $13,000 but the bulls do not seem to be in a hurry to close their positions. If the pair does not drop below $12,460 within the next few days, it will increase the possibility of a rally to $14,000.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the bears can pull the price below the $12,460\u8211\'20\'13$12,050 support zone, it will suggest a lack of demand at higher levels. Such a move will suggest that the current breakout was a bear trap.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) broke out and closed above $395 on Oct. 22. This move completed the ascending triangle pattern, which has a target objective of $478.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/927b02dc-e44c-49a3-92b7-4bf18089fdfe.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising 20-day EMA ($377) and the RSI in the positive territory suggest that the bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are currently trying to pull the price back below the breakout level of $395. If they succeed, it will signal that the current breakout was a fake one. The next support on the downside is the uptrend line.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the ETH/USD pair rebounds off $395, it will suggest that the breakout is valid. The uptrend could pick up momentum after the bulls push the price above $421.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  attempted to rise above the $0.2295\u8211\'20\'13$0.26 range on Oct. 21 but the bulls could not close the price above $0.26. This suggests a lack of buyers at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/324fb92a-f552-45f4-a774-5634efa358b9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The failure of the XRP/USD pair to break out of the range could have attracted profit booking. If the price breaks below the moving averages, it will suggest that the range-bound action is likely to extend for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA ($0.24), the bulls will once again attempt to drive the pair above the $0.26\u8211\'20\'13$0.265763 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close (UTC time) above the resistance zone will complete an inverted head and shoulders pattern that could signal the start of a new uptrend with a target objective of $0.30.\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) is currently facing selling near the overhead resistance at $280. This shows that the bears are trying to keep the price below this level. If they succeed, a drop to the 20-day EMA ($247) is possible.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/6f23e6dc-c03b-4faf-8386-3a172d661d9b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BCH/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BCHUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI close to the oversold zone suggest that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $280, a move to $300 is possible. This level could act as resistance but if the bulls can thrust the price above it, the BCH/USD pair could resume the uptrend and reach $326.30\u8211\'20\'13$337.90.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the pair turns down from the current levels and breaks below the critical support at $242.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke above the downtrend line on Oct. 22. This suggests that the correction could be over. The upsloping moving averages and the RSI above 56 suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/618dddf6-7b3e-46ab-b81c-14baffe5bfcb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the bulls can push the price above $31.9798, a retest of the 52-week high at $33.3888 is possible. A breakout and close above this level could resume the uptrend that can challenge the all-time high at $39.5941.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price continues to decline from the current levels and plummet below $28.50. Such a move could start a deeper correction to $22.\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) completed an ascending triangle pattern when it broke and closed above $11.8028 on Oct. 22. The target objective of this \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup is $15.\par \par \uc2 The gradually upsloping 20-day EMA ($10.71) and the RSI above 57 suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/c34a5af9-66e5-44f5-a6df-5b7cd4e8189d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are not willing to let bulls have their way. They are currently attempting to drag the price back below the $11.199\u8211\'20\'13$11.8028 support zone. If they manage to do that, it will suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the bears fail to sustain the price below the support zone, it will indicate that the bulls are accumulating on dips. This could increase the possibility of a rally to $13.28 and higher.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) closed above the 20-day EMA ($4.17) on Oct. 22. The bulls will now try to push the price above the overhead resistance at $4.6112. A close above this resistance could drive the price to $5.5899.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/e55c8b03-6643-4c85-b5c0-7299f3918086.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI has risen above the 50 levels for the first time in more than a month. This suggests that the selling pressure has reduced and the bulls are attempting to make a comeback.\par \par \uc2 However, if the price again slips back below the 20-day EMA, the DOT/USD pair could extend its stay inside the range for a few more days. The pair may turn negative if the bears sink the pair below the critical support at $3.5321.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) completed an inverse head and shoulders pattern when it broke out and closed above the $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36 resistance zone. The pattern target of this \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal setup is $61.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/501c51e1-b8f9-45e8-acb4-8b229a3dba5e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA ($49) and the RSI near the overbought zone suggest that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 However, after the initial run-up, the price may retest the breakout zone of $51\u8211\'20\'13$52.36. If the bulls purchase the dip to this zone and the price recovers sharply, it will suggest that the zone may act as a floor in the future.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the bears drag and sustain the LTC/USD pair below $51. Such a move will suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been trading inside a rising wedge pattern for the past few days. The bulls have failed to push the price above the immediate resistance at $0.1142241, which shows a lack of demand at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/4e039054-a3f2-4f7c-be98-586188cafb02.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising wedge is usually considered as a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. The pattern will complete when the price drops and closes below the support line of the wedge. Such a move could drag the price down to $0.090 and then to $0.0755701.\par \par \uc2 However, the upsloping 20-day EMA ($0.10) and the RSI in the positive zone suggest a minor advantage to the bulls. If the buyers can propel the price above the wedge, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD pair could start an up-move that may reach $0.01445.\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin SV ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/bitcoin-sv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BSV}}}\uc2  ) has formed a symmetrical triangle pattern, which shows indecision among the bulls and the bears. Although the bulls had pushed the price above the triangle on Oct. 22, they could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2020-10/5f63b269-1eaf-4634-9116-913b89fc683e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BSV/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BSVUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The price has turned down from the downtrend line and the bears will now try to sink the BSV/USD pair to the uptrend line of the triangle. If this support cracks, a drop to $146.20 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the pair rebounds off the uptrend line, the bulls will once again attempt to push the price above the triangle. If they can pull it off, a rally to $180.63 and then to $227 could be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5ldS1jZW50cmFsLTEuYW1hem9uYXdzLmNvbS9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjAtMTAvYzBlZWY4OTQtZDJkZS00NzM1LWExNGItNWQ0OTEwODEwNjAwLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020201024egan0005p\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\i